{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794570168606,"sessionID":"ses_e2b4a23c4ffeXM7ei3r7kNeMRl","part":{"partID":"prt_1d4b7a8bb002rf4uUFKSOHQpV2","sessionID":"ses_e2b4a23c4ffeXM7ei3r7kNeMRl","messageID":"msg_1d4b79ad6001CKDKEBLkuwtjDa","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-bd526ad555fcb866","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-report-pass-1.md","offset":140,"limit":180},"output":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/review-report-pass-1.md, lines 140-319\n140: }\n141: ```\n142: \n143: ---\n144: \n145: ## 3. Active Finding Registry\n146: \n147: ### 3.1 Full table (43 merged findings plus 3 queued items)\n148: \n149: Verdict key: CONFIRMED means the defect is real as stated. ADJUSTED means real but the severity or the description is corrected. REFUTED means the code does not do what the finding says. Origin is from `git blame` against `35c3188681`: introduced means the cited lines came from the reviewed range, pre-existing means they predate it.\n150: \n151: | Id | Sev after (before) | Verdict | Location | Origin | Fix in one line |\n152: |---|---|---|---|---|---|\n153: | DR1-P1-001 | P2 (P1) | ADJUSTED | `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs:1364` | pre-existing | Catch a throw in the write loop, call `restoreFromBackup`, print the backup and undo lines and return a distinct exit the workflow reads as undone |\n154: | DR4-P1-001 | P2 (P1) | ADJUSTED | `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs:783` | pre-existing | Throw `PreconditionError` in `compose` when `REPO RULES.md` or `.cursor/rules/repo-local.md` is a symlink, as `:652` does for the root document |\n155: | DR4-P2-001 | P2 | CONFIRMED | `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs:1289` | pre-existing | Run `assertWritable` and the per-entry sha256 check inside `restoreFromBackup`, as `commandRestore` already does |\n156: | DR1-P2-003 | P2 | CONFIRMED | `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs:598` | pre-existing | Fail plan and apply on a non-empty `foreign` list exactly as they fail on `dropped` |\n157: | R2-P2-001 | P2 | CONFIRMED | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:353` | introduced | Return no command from `attachCommand` when the shared no-edit pattern matches |\n158: | R1-P2-001 | P2 | ADJUSTED | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:385` | introduced | Open the deep-loop gate only when the typed `/deep:` command equals the command being attached |\n159: | R1-P2-002--95282927956e | P2 | CONFIRMED | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:266` | introduced | Treat a `/` or a `.` followed by a word character after the key as a continuation so a file name never matches |\n160: | R4-P2-001--d1528b81a2ca | P2 | CONFIRMED | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:123` | introduced | Delete the `COMMAND_POLICIES` emitter and block, because the live reader `TRACKED_COMMANDS` covers 11 attachable commands it lacks |\n161: | R4-P2-002--828881666f76 | P2 | CONFIRMED | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts:750` | pre-existing | Delete the empty semantic-search branch |\n162: | R1-P2-005 | P2 | CONFIRMED | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts:226` | introduced | Skip the row backfill in `commandLabel` when `needsMode` is true |\n163: | R2-P2-003 | P2 | ADJUSTED | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts:233` | introduced | Read `mutating` from the row whose command equals the printed command and treat an unknown command as writing |\n164: | R4-P2-002--de3d8b259d8e | P2 | CONFIRMED | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts:522` | introduced | Keep the literal and add a parity test against `isChildSession` in `spec-gate-core.mjs` instead of a cross-package import |\n165: | Q1 (queued item i) | P2 | CONFIRMED | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-brief-golden.vitest.ts`, `tests/hooks/skill-advisor-cli-fallback-envelope.vitest.ts` | introduced | Stub `AI_SESSION_CHILD` to an empty string in `beforeEach` and unstub in `afterEach`, as `render-child-session.vitest.ts` does |\n166: | iter5-P2-credential-hardening-allowlist | P2 | CONFIRMED | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs:782` | introduced | Build the child environment from an allowlist instead of deleting three GitHub token names |\n167: | iter2-P2-arena-precondition-unverified | P2 | CONFIRMED | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs:986` | introduced | Have the arena builder write a marker and refuse a live arm when it is missing |\n168: | iter4-P2-g2-label-grammar-duplication | P2 | CONFIRMED | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:929` | introduced | Export the g2 row map from the runner and label rows from it instead of from a regex |\n169: | DR1-P2-001 | P2 | CONFIRMED | `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs:709` | pre-existing | Consult `expectsAbsent` before the symlink branch |\n170: | DR1-P2-002 | P2 | CONFIRMED | `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs:731` | pre-existing | Reword the pass detail to say the file names the root document and carries no shipped line |\n171: | DR3-P2-001 | P2 | CONFIRMED | `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs:649` | introduced | Leave the pointer-missing entry out of the \"as expected\" count and count it on its own |\n172: | DR5-P2-003 | P2 | CONFIRMED | `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs:809` | pre-existing | Report a width-mismatched router row as malformed with its line instead of dropping it |\n173: | DR3-P2-004 | P2 | CONFIRMED | `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/README.markdown:102` | pre-existing | Say four children and name the A12 manifest generator here and in the module header |\n174: | DR5-P2-001 | P2 | CONFIRMED | `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/codex-hook-approval-check.cjs:59` | introduced | Reject a flag value that starts with `-`, as `hook-wiring-check.cjs:87` does |\n175: | DR5-P2-002 | P2 | CONFIRMED | `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/hook-wiring-check.cjs:123` | introduced | Match the marker as the script path inside a `type: command` entry's `command`, never in the serialized payload |\n176: | DR3-P2-002 | P2 | CONFIRMED | `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-runtime-mirrors.yaml:165` | introduced | Print a repair line in the absent branch and route setup to that line instead of to `/doctor:runtime-mirrors` |\n177: | DR3-P2-003 | P2 | CONFIRMED | `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-symlink-check.yaml:67` | introduced | Add the hook-wiring exit 1 to the output block as WARN |\n178: | DR2-P2-003 | P2 | CONFIRMED | `.skilled/commands/doctor/setup.md:75` | pre-existing | Name the socket-directory write in the workflow's mutation boundary or drop it from `setup.md` |\n179: | Q3 (queued item iii) | P2 | CONFIRMED | `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml:59` | introduced | Print \"hook health not recorded\" with the reason when `data.hookHealth` is absent |\n180: | DR2-P2-001 | P2 | ADJUSTED | `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-install-presentation.txt:78` | pre-existing | Replace \"the seven\" with the six names plus \"the ones already there\" and record the missing dsh install row as a decision |\n181: | DR2-P2-002 | P2 | CONFIRMED | `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-skill-advisor-embedder.yaml:89` | introduced | Run `ollama serve` and `ollama pull` with `OLLAMA_HOST` taken from the resolved URL. Otherwise refuse start and pull for a non-local URL |\n182: | iter5-P2-holdout-secondary-split-publication | P2 | CONFIRMED | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs:537` | introduced | Leave holdout rows out of the published `rows` map and compare only non-holdout rows in the slice test |\n183: | iter1-P2-readme-inventory-drift | P2 | CONFIRMED | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:29` | introduced | Set the count to 14 and list every code and data file |\n184: | iter3-P2-readme-restore-exit3 | P2 | CONFIRMED | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:113` | introduced | Document exit 3 (`head_moved`) and that it skips the restore |\n185: | iter1-P2-offer-reached-unknown | P2 | ADJUSTED | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/README.md:111` | introduced | Reword the README: `offerReached` counts offers whose brief was not shown missing, so `unknown` counts |\n186: | R1-P2-004 | P2 | CONFIRMED | `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/devin.mjs:395` | pre-existing | Fall through to `loadTranscript` before returning `store_unreadable` on a database open or projection failure |\n187: | R1-P2-003 | P2 | ADJUSTED | `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/dsh.mjs:195` | pre-existing | Keep the fail-closed rule and pin it with a test and a reader README sentence |\n188: | R1-P2-002--fabc628596e7 | P2 | ADJUSTED | `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/claude.mjs:217` | pre-existing | Open `containment.path` instead of the caller path in the claude, devin, dsh and pi readers |\n189: | R4-P2-001--09ff48e9a0b9 | P2 | CONFIRMED | `.skilled/hooks/shared/session-readers/index.mjs:28` | pre-existing | Add `Object.keys(capabilities)` to the runtime list parity test |\n190: | R2-P2-002 | P2 | CONFIRMED | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/subprocess.ts:239` | pre-existing | Cap stdout and stderr the way `capStdout` caps them in the hook fallback |\n191: | iter4-P2-bench-runtime-matrix-incomplete | P2 | CONFIRMED | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/bench/hook-brief-signal-noise.bench.ts:26` | pre-existing | Fill the matrix for every value in `ADVISOR_RUNTIME_VALUES` |\n192: | R3-P2-001--0e0d904eb571 | P2 | CONFIRMED | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/README.md:176` | introduced | Say 46 rows here and in `feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md:26` |\n193: | R3-P2-002--5522ea1fe8dd | P2 | CONFIRMED | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/ARCHITECTURE.md:142` | pre-existing | Add the DSH prompt adapter (`hooks/dsh/prompt-advisor.mjs`) to the adapter sentence |\n194: | R3-P2-002--ecbea1260371 | P2 | ADJUSTED | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md:45` | introduced | Add `mutating` to the documented row shape and name it as the child downgrade's input |\n195: | Q2 (queued item ii) | P2 | CONFIRMED | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md:45` | introduced | Name `TRACKED_COMMANDS[command].policy` as the attach-path policy source |\n196: | R4-P2-003 | P2 | CONFIRMED | `AGENTS.md:65` | pre-existing | Show the direct call with `--json -` and the request on stdin |\n197: | iter3-P2-phase007-open-evidence | P2 | CONFIRMED | `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/spec.md:120` | introduced | Close phase 007 or record in the phase map why phases 10 to 13 closed past it |\n198: | R3-P2-001--16e5737e0e56 | none | REFUTED | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md:176` | pre-existing | No change |\n199: \n200: ### 3.2 Verified scenarios for the two former P1 findings\n201: \n202: **DR1-P1-001, `agents-md-embed.cjs:1364`, lowered to P2.**\n203: \n204: - Input: the `claude-only` fixture (a repository with only `CLAUDE.md`), `plan --create-router`, then `apply --plan-digest <digest> --create-router` with the second write failing. The probe used the engine's own `hooks.write` seam to throw `EACCES` on the second call.\n205: - What happens: `AGENTS.md` is created, then the throw leaves the bare loop at `:1365-1374`. `main` re-throws it because it is not an allowlist, precondition or usage error (`:1562-1572`), so the CLI's outer catch prints `ERROR: <message>` and exits 2 (`:1579-1581`). No restore runs and apply prints no backup or undo line. The probe tree after the run held `AGENTS.md` and the untouched `CLAUDE.md`. The workflow then reads exit 2 as \"nothing was written\" (`doctor-agents-md-embed.yaml:100` and `:104`), which is false here.\n206: - What should happen: the loop catches the throw, calls `restoreFromBackup`, prints the backup and undo lines and ends with STATUS=FAIL under an exit code the workflow maps to \"the run was undone\".\n207: - Why P2 and not P1: reach needs an I/O fault on an allowlisted path after every precondition passed. The shapes a link install produces are refused before any byte (probe: a `REPO RULES.md` linked outside the root exits 2 with \"resolves outside the target root through a link, nothing was written\"). The backup is complete before the first write (`:1361`) and the plan the operator approved already printed `backup:` and `undo:` (`:1228-1230`), so nothing is lost. It is a recoverability gap, not a wrong result on a default path.\n208: - Test: in `agents-md-embed.test.cjs`, a write hook that throws on the second call. Today `main` throws and `AGENTS.md` stays. After the fix `main` returns non-zero with `restored` and `undo:` in its output. `treeDigest` then equals the pre-run digest.\n209: \n210: **DR4-P1-001, `agents-md-embed.cjs:783`, lowered to P2.**\n211: \n212: - Input: `.cursor/rules/repo-local.md` is a symlink to `../../.github/ci.yml` inside the repository and the block carries content (probe on the `foreign` fixture).\n213: - What happens: plan prints `target .cursor/rules/repo-local.md: replace` with a diff whose before side is the CI file's bytes. Apply writes the mirror text through the link into `.github/ci.yml` and ends `STATUS=OK`. A second probe with `REPO RULES.md` linked to an in-root table file wrote the added router row into that file. The backup recorded `symlink: true`.\n214: - What should happen: compose refuses a symlinked router or mirror the way it refuses a symlinked root document (`:652-654`).\n215: - Why P2 and not P1: the finding's own case is wrong. It says the link install mode produces `REPO RULES.md -> AGENTS.md`, but `symlink-manifest.json:24` links `REPO RULES.md` to the Skilled checkout's own file and `:8` links `.cursor` to the checkout's folder. Both resolve outside the target root. `assertWritable` (`:900-904`) refuses them before any backup (probe exit 2). A `REPO RULES.md` linked to `AGENTS.md` is a no-op because `AGENTS.md` has no trigger table (probe: router `unchanged`). What remains is a hand-made link inside the root, whose bytes the plan's diff shows and the backup restores. No security boundary is crossed.\n216: - Test: a fixture whose mirror links to an in-root file. Today plan exits 0 and lists `replace`. After the fix plan exits 2 and names the link with its target. The linked file stays unchanged.\n217: \n218: ### 3.3 Verified scenarios for the safety-shaped P2 findings\n219: \n220: **R2-P2-001, `command-attach.ts:353`, hub attach ignores a no-edit request. Reach proven.**\n221: \n222: - Input: the prompt \"use sk-doc to create a skill called invoice-parser, do not change anything yet\" with `SPECKIT_COMPILED_ROUTING` unset (`sk-doc` is in `DEFAULT_ON_HUBS`, `compiled-routing-flag.ts:32-40`).\n223: - What happens: `compiled-route.cjs --hub sk-doc` returns `route/single/sk-create-skill` for this and three other no-edit prompts (probe). The full `advisor_recommend` call returns `sk-doc` at 0.8932 with `command: /create:skill` and `policy: start` (probe). The scorer path rules out every command on the same wording (`fusion.ts:887`).\n224: - What should happen: `attachCommand` returns no command when `NO_EDIT_REQUEST` matches.\n225: - Why it stays P2: `start` makes the command's setup ask before writing. `AGENTS.md:68` also says an explicit instruction outranks the policy. A transcript in which a runtime starts the writing steps on such a prompt would raise it to P1.\n226: - Test: `attachCommand('sk-doc', <single sk-create-skill route>, '<the prompt above>')` returns `/create:skill` today and `undefined` after.\n227: \n228: **R1-P2-001, `command-attach.ts:385`, any `/deep:` mention opens the deep-loop gate. Reach narrowed.**\n229: \n230: - Input: a single-mode review route and the prompt \"what did /deep:ai-council decide\".\n231: - What happens: `attachCommand` returns `/deep:review` (probe). On the top recommendation `attachTypedCommand` then replaces it with the typed `/deep:ai-council` (probe of `typedCommandForTop`), which masks the bug in the common case. It still reaches the reader when the `/deep:` text names no tracked command (a typo such as `/deep:reviw`) or when a lower recommendation is enriched (`compiledRouteTopOnly` false, which the prompt hooks never send).\n232: - What should happen: the gate opens only when the typed `/deep:` command equals the command being attached.\n233: - Test: the call above returns `/deep:review` today and `undefined` after, while \"run /deep:review now\" still returns `/deep:review`.\n234: \n235: **R1-P2-002--95282927956e, `command-attach.ts:266`, a file name reads as a typed command.**\n236: \n237: - Input: \"open /create:readme.md and summarise it\" with `sk-doc` on top.\n238: - What happens: `typedCommandIn` returns `/create:readme` and `typedCommandForTop` returns it with `policy: start` (probe), so a request to read a file is offered a writing command.\n239: - What should happen: a `/` or a `.` followed by a word character after the key cancels the match. A sentence-ending period still ends a command.\n240: - Test: `typedCommandIn('see /create:skill.md for details')` returns `/create:skill` today and `undefined` after, while `typedCommandIn('run /create:skill.')` keeps returning `/create:skill`.\n241: \n242: **R1-P2-005, `render.ts:226`, `needsMode` is overridden by a generated row. Latent.**\n243: \n244: - Input: `renderAdvisorBrief` with a top recommendation `{ skill: 'command-create-agent', needsMode: true }` and no `command`.\n245: - What happens: the head reads `use sk-doc → /create:agent (start)` (probe on the built renderer) instead of `(needs a mode)`.\n246: - Reach: none today. `needsMode` is set only for hubs in `MODE_COMMANDS` (`command-attach.ts:394-399`) and no hub id has a command row (probe returned an empty list).\n247: - What should happen: `commandLabel` skips the row backfill when `needsMode` is true.\n248: - Test: the input above prints `/create:agent` today and `(needs a mode)` after.\n249: \n250: **R2-P2-003, `render.ts:233`, the child downgrade reads the wrong row. Latent.**\n251: \n252: - Input: a child session and `{ skill: 'command-speckit-search', command: '/doctor:speckit', policy: 'run' }`. The skill's row is `run` and `read-only`, while `/doctor:speckit` is `run` and `add-only` (`command-attach.ts:105`).\n253: - What happens: the head reads `/doctor:speckit (run)` in the child (probe) where `(parent-named only)` is due.\n254: - Adjustment: the lineage's example (`sk-doc` with `/doctor:overlay apply`) does not reproduce. `sk-doc` has no row and `/doctor:overlay apply` is `ask`, so the pair renders `(parent-named only)`. No producer pairs a command with another command's row today. A recommendation with no row already downgrades (probe).\n255: - Test: the input above prints `(run)` today and `(parent-named only)` after.\n256: \n257: **iter1-P2-offer-reached-unknown, `score-command-transcripts.mjs:1293`, adjusted to a README defect.**\n258: \n259: - Input: an OpenCode run log, whose brief state is always `unknown` (`command-offer.mjs:207-208`), with an offered command on each row.\n260: - What happens: `offerReached` equals `offered`, because the tally counts `briefDelivered !== false`.\n261: - Adjustment: this is the rule the packet specified. Phase 013 task T022 says \"add 1 to a new `offerReached` when `result.offered` and `result.briefDelivered !== false`\". SC-002 pins OpenCode at `offerReached` 3 with `deliveryUnknown` 24. The code is right. The README line at `:111` (\"offers on a turn whose brief arrived\") is wrong.\n262: - Test: no code change, so no failing test. The phase 013 SC-002 summary pin already holds the rule.\n263: \n264: **iter5-P2-credential-hardening-allowlist, `run-command-behaviour.mjs:782`.**\n265: \n266: - Input: an operator shell with `SSH_AUTH_SOCK`, an AWS profile and `NPM_TOKEN` set runs `--runtime claude --set g2 --out <log>` from a prepared arena.\n267: - What happens: `childEnv` copies `process.env` and removes only `GH_TOKEN`, `GITHUB_TOKEN` and `GH_ENTERPRISE_TOKEN` (`:782-789`). The turn runs with `--permission-mode bypassPermissions` (`:126`), so a shell step in it can use the SSH agent, the npm token or the cloud profile.\n268: - What should happen: the child environment is built from an allowlist (path, home, locale, terminal, temp folder and the runtime's own configuration and provider key) or the runner refuses a live arm while such variables are set.\n269: - Why P2: the header's stated threat is a push through this repository's remote. The remote guard at `:986-992` closes it. No fixture prompt asks for network work.\n270: - Test: export `childEnv` and assert `SSH_AUTH_SOCK`, `AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID` and `NPM_TOKEN` are absent from its result. Today they are present.\n271: \n272: **iter2-P2-arena-precondition-unverified, `run-command-behaviour.mjs:986`.**\n273: \n274: - Input: a local checkout after `git remote remove origin`, clean status, with an ignored `.env` and outer git hooks, then a live arm.\n275: - What happens: `remoteNames()` is empty and the dirty check passes, so turns with bypassed permissions run in a tree that never went through `prepare-behaviour-arena.mjs` and its dotenv and hook refusals.\n276: - What should happen: the arena builder writes a marker under the clone's `.git` folder and the first-turn guard refuses a live arm without it (`EXIT_REFUSED`, code `arena_unprepared`).\n277: - Test: a temporary repository with no remote and no marker passes the guard today and returns `arena_unprepared` after.\n278: \n279: ### 3.4 Evidence and tests for the remaining findings\n280: \n281: Each line gives the evidence read in this synthesis and a test that fails today and passes after. Where no such test can exist, the line says so.\n282: \n283: - **DR4-P2-001** `restoreFromBackup` (`:1284-1305`) copies with `path.join` and `copyFileSync` only, while `commandRestore` runs `assertWritable` and the sha256 check (`:1453`, `:1464`). Test: a write hook that damages the backup copy of `AGENTS.md` and drops a line. Today the damaged bytes are restored silently, after the restore stops on the hash mismatch and says so.\n284: - **DR1-P2-003** `foreign` is built at `:587-596` and read only by unit tests (`agents-md-embed.test.cjs:395-974`). Test: a write hook that adds a line above the block. Today apply ends `STATUS=OK`, after it ends `STATUS=FAIL` with a restore.\n285: - **R4-P2-001--d1528b81a2ca** The only `COMMAND_POLICIES` references are its declaration, its emitter (`derive-command-bridges.cjs:1218`) and prose. `advisor-recommend.ts:478` reads `TRACKED_COMMANDS`. A probe found 11 tracked commands missing from `COMMAND_POLICIES`. All 11 are reachable through `MODE_COMMANDS` (`/create:benchmark`, `/create:command`, `/create:diff`, `/create:goal`, `/create:repo-rule`, `/create:skill-parent`, `/create:with-human-voice`, `/deep:ai-council`, `/design:chart`, `/design:diagram` and `/design:extract`). So the scorer lineage's preferred fix (point the attach path at `COMMAND_POLICIES`) would strip the policy from those 11. Delete it instead. Test: `'COMMAND_POLICIES' in await import('../lib/command-attach.js')` is true today and false after, with the deriver's check mode still exiting 0.\n286: - **R4-P2-002--828881666f76** `fusion.ts:750-751` is an `if` with an empty body. Test: none can fail, because removing it changes no output. The scorer suite is the guard.\n287: - **R4-P2-002--de3d8b259d8e** `render.ts:522` compares the literal while `spec-gate-core.mjs:101-106` exports the constant and `isChildSession`. Both accept exactly `'1'` today. Test: a parity test over `'1'`, `'0'`, `'true'` and an empty value. It passes today and guards the drift the finding describes.\n288: - **Q1 (queued item i)** Both files call `renderAdvisorBrief` with no `childSession` option, so `render.ts:522` reads the caller's environment. Under `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1` the built renderer turns `/create:readme (start)` into `(parent-named only)` (probe). The golden file asserts eight `expectedHead` values with `(start)` or `(ask)` plus the ambiguous head. The envelope file asserts one. That makes 10, which matches the coordinator's 10 failures. Without the variable both files pass (12 of 12 and 3 of 3, exit 0). Test: the two files run under `AI_SESSION_CHILD=1` fail today and pass after.\n289: - **iter4-P2-g2-label-grammar-duplication** The runner defines six ids (`run-command-behaviour.mjs:678-698`) and `assertRunnable` accepts any of them (`:724-727`). The scorer rebuilds labels from `STARTED_ROW` (`score-command-transcripts.mjs:929`) and returns `unknown_row` on a miss (`:1156`). All six current ids match. Test: an id added to the shared map outside the regex grammar scores `unknown_row` today and its label after.\n290: - **DR1-P2-001** `copyVerdict` returns `PASS / symlink` at `:709-713` before `expectsAbsent` is read. Probe: `.codex/AGENTS.md -> ../AGENTS.md` reported `PASS symlink`. Test: that tree reports `PASS` today and `FINDING` after.\n291: - **DR1-P2-002** `namesRoot` uses `.some` (`:727`) while the detail at `:731` says every line. Test: a `CLAUDE.md` holding the pointer and one local line reports \"every line names\" today and the corrected wording after.\n292: - **DR3-P2-001** The INFO branch added at `:693-700` is excluded from `failed` and `unmeasured` (`:646-649`). Probe: a tree without `CLAUDE.md` reported `5/6 copies as expected` with the INFO entry inside the five and its `pointer missing` line printed beneath. Test: that tree counts the INFO entry as expected today and separately after.\n293: - **DR5-P2-003** `parseTableRows` drops a row whose width differs (`agents-md-check.cjs:809`) while `addRouterRows` keys rows by rule path with no width check (`agents-md-embed.cjs:329-330`, `:361`). Test: a router row with a literal pipe in its summary reports a missing trigger row today and a malformed row with its line after.\n294: - **DR3-P2-004** `defaultTools` wires four children (`:875-884`) and `spawnSync` runs at `:447`, `:666`, `:768` and `:859`. The README row and the header at `:15` say three. Test: a doc check that the count word equals the `defaultTools` entry count fails today.\n295: - **DR5-P2-001** Probe: `codex-hook-approval-check.cjs --root --json` printed `SKIP no-codex-hooks` and exited 0, while `hook-wiring-check.cjs --root --json` refused with usage. Test: the first call exits 0 today and 2 after.\n296: - **DR5-P2-002** `JSON.stringify(payload).includes(runtime.marker)` at `:123`. Probe: a `.claude/settings.json` whose only prompt entry is `echo hooks/claude/user-prompt-submit.js` printed `ok claude`. Test: an entry that names the marker only in a `description` field reports `ok` today and `hook-missing` after.\n297: - **DR3-P2-002** The absent branch (`codex-hook-approval-check.cjs:171-179`) prints no `repair` line, `doctor-runtime-mirrors.yaml:165-166` promises one and `doctor-setup.yaml:61` routes the state to `/doctor:runtime-mirrors`, whose Codex row only reads. WG6 adds this line and WG7 routes to it: `repair: copy the advisor UserPromptSubmit entry from the Skilled checkout's .codex/hooks.json into <root>/.codex/hooks.json, then approve it with /hooks in a Codex session`. Test: a hooks file without the advisor entry prints no `repair:` today and prints it after.\n298: - **DR3-P2-003** The output block (`doctor-symlink-check.yaml:66-69`) maps only the engine's exits. The step at `:60`, added in this range, ends WARN on hook exit 1. Test: a contract assertion that the output block names the hook check's exit 1 fails today.\n299: - **DR2-P2-003** `setup.md:75` allows one out-of-repository write while `doctor-setup.yaml:23-28` declares `allowed_targets: []` and forbids `**/*`. Test: a contract assertion that the workflow boundary names the socket directory fails today.\n300: - **Q3 (queued item iii)** `doctor-setup.yaml:59` shows hook health only when `data.hookHealth` is present. `advisor-status.ts:487-501` adds it only when diagnostic records exist. `persistAdvisorHookDiagnosticRecord` writes them only when `SKILL_ADVISOR_DEBUG` is set (`metrics.ts:320`, `:450`). The opt-in was a deliberate v0.3.0.0 decision, so the smallest fix is in the setup text, not in the writer. Test: a contract assertion that the advisor leg names the absent case fails today.\n301: - **DR2-P2-001** \"the seven\" at `:78` can be read as the six names plus \"the ones already there\", which `:71` accepts. `symlink-manifest.json` has no `dsh` row, so the guide matches the engine. The residual defect is the ambiguous count and no install path for dsh. Test: a contract assertion that the count word equals the listed accepted values fails today.\n302: - **DR2-P2-002** The probe step reads `OLLAMA_BASE_URL` (`:89`) while the start and pull steps (`:125-126`) bind no host. Test: a contract assertion that both mutating steps name `OLLAMA_HOST` from the resolved URL fails today.\n303: - **iter5-P2-holdout-secondary-split-publication** `rows[row.id]` at `:537` writes every row. The committed baseline holds 176 rows, of which 44 have ids marked holdout (ids counted, no prompt text read). `command-routing-slice.vitest.ts:91-107` compares them all and tells the developer to recapture. `holdout-independent.vitest.ts:5-18` names this split a secondary signal, while `spec.md:144` still uses it as acceptance evidence. Test: an assertion that no baseline row id belongs to the holdout split finds 44 today and 0 after.\n304: - **iter1-P2-readme-inventory-drift** The folder holds 14 code files (13 `.mjs` and one `.py`) against \"9\" at `:29`. It held 8 before the range. Test: a doc check comparing the count with the folder fails today.\n305: - **iter3-P2-readme-restore-exit3** `EXIT_HEAD_MOVED = 3` (`run-command-behaviour.mjs:69`) and the head-moved branch skips the restore (`:1032-1037`). The README row at `:113` lists only exit 2 and an unconditional restore. Test: a doc check that the README names exit 3 fails today.\n306: - **R1-P2-004** On an open failure (`devin.mjs:399-404`) or a projection failure (`:419-420`, `:438-440`) the loader returns `store_unreadable` without trying `loadTranscript` (`:447`). This matches the reader README's code table, so it is a design gap. Test: a corrupt `sessions.db` beside an intact transcript returns `store_unreadable` today and `ok` after.\n307: - **R1-P2-003** `dsh.mjs:195` keeps a record only for `source.kind === 'user'`. The injected list added in this range files a sourceless message as `unknown` (`:244-256`), which the reader README documents at `:36`. Whether DSH ever emits a sourceless operator message is not shown. Test: a sourceless `user/message` lands in `injected` with source `unknown`. It passes today and pins the documented rule.\n308: - **R1-P2-002--fabc628596e7** `claude.mjs:213` records `containment.path` and `:217` opens `transcriptPath`. For a link both name the same file, so the two can differ only if the path is swapped between check and open inside the user's own store. The lineage's claim that `pi.mjs` already closes the gap is wrong: it also reads `filePath` after the guard (`pi.mjs:245-256`). Test: no deterministic failing test, because the gap is a race.\n309: - **R4-P2-001--09ff48e9a0b9** `capabilities` (`index.mjs:28-65`) spells seven runtimes and no test compares it with `ADVISOR_RUNTIME_VALUES`. Today the two sets agree. Test: the added comparison passes today and fails the day a runtime is added to one list only.\n310: - **R2-P2-002** `stdout += chunk` with no ceiling (`subprocess.ts:238-243`), while the hook fallback caps at 1 MiB (`skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts:92`, `:214-218`). Only the timeout bounds it. Test: a fake child writing 2 MiB yields 2 MiB today and at most the cap after.\n311: - **iter4-P2-bench-runtime-matrix-incomplete** Run with `SPECKIT_RUN_BENCHES=true`, the bench file failed one of four tests with `TypeError: Cannot convert undefined or null to object` at `:95` (exit 1). The runtime tuple already held seven values before the range, when the matrix had three, so the gap predates the packet. Test: the bench file itself fails today and passes after.\n312: - **R3-P2-001--0e0d904eb571** `counts.typescriptActive` is 46 and 46 entries carry `embeddingText` in `command-bridges.generated.json`. Both 45 sentences came from the range. Test: a doc check against `counts.typescriptActive` fails today.\n313: - **R3-P2-002--5522ea1fe8dd** `hooks/dsh/prompt-advisor.mjs` ships a DSH adapter and predates the range. The sentence at `:142` names five adapters plus the plugin. Test: a doc check that every adapter folder under `hooks/` is named fails today.\n314: - **R3-P2-002--ecbea1260371** The four-field recommendation contract at `:41-43` is accurate, since the output carries no `mutating`. The defect is `:45`, which gives the row shape as `{ command, policy?, ownerSkillId }` while `command-attach.ts:51` adds `mutating`, the field `render.ts:233` reads. Test: a doc check that `:45` names every `CommandRow` field fails today.\n315: - **Q2 (queued item ii)** `advisor-recommend.md:45` says the compiled-route attach takes its policy from `COMMAND_POLICIES[command]`. The code reads `TRACKED_COMMANDS[command].policy` (`advisor-recommend.ts:478`). Test: the doc check above, extended to the policy source,