does for the root document |\n155: | DR4-P2-001 | P2 | CONFIRMED | `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs:1289` | pre-existing | Run `assertWritable` and the per-entry sha256 check inside `restoreFromBackup`, as `commandRestore` already does |\n156: | DR1-P2-003 | P2 | CONFIRMED | `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-embed.cjs:598` | pre-existing | Fail plan and apply on a non-empty `foreign` list exactly as they fail on `dropped` |\n157: | R2-P2-001 | P2 | CONFIRMED | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:353` | introduced | Return no command from `attachCommand` when the shared no-edit pattern matches |\n158: | R1-P2-001 | P2 | ADJUSTED | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:385` | introduced | Open the deep-loop gate only when the typed `/deep:` command equals the command being attached |\n159: | R1-P2-002--95282927956e | P2 | CONFIRMED | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:266` | introduced | Treat a `/` or a `.` followed by a word character after the key as a continuation so a file name never matches |\n160: | R4-P2-001--d1528b81a2ca | P2 | CONFIRMED | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:123` | introduced | Delete the `COMMAND_POLICIES` emitter and block, because the live reader `TRACKED_COMMANDS` covers 11 attachable commands it lacks |\n161: | R4-P2-002--828881666f76 | P2 | CONFIRMED | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts:750` | pre-existing | Delete the empty semantic-search branch |\n162: | R1-P2-005 | P2 | CONFIRMED | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts:226` | introduced | Skip the row backfill in `commandLabel` when `needsMode` is true |\n163: | R2-P2-003 | P2 | ADJUSTED | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts:233` | introduced | Read `mutating` from the row whose command equals the printed command and treat an unknown command as writing |\n164: | R4-P2-002--de3d8b259d8e | P2 | CONFIRMED | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/render.ts:522` | introduced | Keep the literal and add a parity test against `isChildSession` in `spec-gate-core.mjs` instead of a cross-package import |\n165: | Q1 (queued item i) | P2 | CONFIRMED | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-brief-golden.vitest.ts`, `tests/hooks/skill-advisor-cli-fallback-envelope.vitest.ts` | introduced | Stub `AI_SESSION_CHILD` to an empty string in `beforeEach` and unstub in `afterEach`, as `render-child-session.vitest.ts` does |\n166: | iter5-P2-credential-hardening-allowlist | P2 | CONFIRMED | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs:782` | introduced | Build the child environment from an allowlist instead of deleting three GitHub token names |\n167: | iter2-P2-arena-precondition-unverified | P2 | CONFIRMED | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/run-command-behaviour.mjs:986` | introduced | Have the arena builder write a marker and refuse a live arm when it is missing |\n168: | iter4-P2-g2-label-grammar-duplication | P2 | CONFIRMED | `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/score-command-transcripts.mjs:929` | introduced | Export the g2 row map from the runner and label rows from it instead of from a regex |\n169: | DR1-P2-001 | P2 | CONFIRMED | `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs:709` | pre-existing | Consult `expectsAbsent` before the symlink branch |\n170: | DR1-P2-002 | P2 | CONFIRMED | `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs:731` | pre-existing | Reword the pass detail to say the file names the root document and carries no shipped line |\n171: | DR3-P2-001 | P2 | CONFIRMED | `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs:649` | introduced | Leave the pointer-missing entry out of the \"as expected\" count and count it on its own |\n172: | DR5-P2-0