{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794570286847,"sessionID":"ses_e2b4a23c4ffeXM7ei3r7kNeMRl","part":{"partID":"prt_1d4b976be0018clVPI5CA7TiRz","sessionID":"ses_e2b4a23c4ffeXM7ei3r7kNeMRl","messageID":"msg_1d4b96d49001Kmv1alIRtUBX8P","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b96493149e0a60fb","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach/deep-review-strategy.md","offset":78,"limit":120},"output":"Read file specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach/deep-review-strategy.md, lines 78-197\n78: <!-- /ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n79: ## 8. WHAT WORKED\n80: \n81: - Executing the shipped module with `node --experimental-strip-types` turned two boundary questions into executed evidence instead of a reading: the `/deep:` bypass and the `/create:skill.md` match both reproduced exactly (iteration 1).\n82: - Diffing the generated tables against their authored sources (`mode-registry.json`, `_routes.yaml`, `command-metadata.json`) proved three \"missing row\" hypotheses false before they became findings (iteration 1).\n83: - Executing a whole-table invariant instead of reading rows one at a time settled the mutating-command question in one check: 56 rows, 0 `run` with a writing class, 0 policy mismatches between the two generated maps (iteration 2).\n84: \n85: ---\n86: \n87: ## 9. WHAT FAILED\n88: \n89: - Parsing `command-bridges.generated.json` `commandPolicies` as a runnable-keyed map failed: doctor routes are keyed by bare command (`/doctor:git`) while the derived rows key by runnable (`/doctor:git setup`). Discarded that comparison as a methodology error rather than reporting a false drift (iteration 1).\n90: - Importing `lib/scorer/projection.ts` under `--experimental-strip-types` failed on its `.js` specifier (`ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND`), so the bridge-owner completeness check was answered by counting declarations in the file instead of executing it (iteration 2).\n91: \n92: ---\n93: \n94: <!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n95: ## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n96: [No exhausted approach categories. No review approach was retried after failing; the hypotheses that were eliminated are single-pass ruled-out directions, listed under \"Ruled Out Directions\" below and enumerated with evidence in `deep-review-dashboard.md` section 10 and the registry `ruledOutCandidates`.]\n97: <!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n98: ## 10A. SATURATED / SWEPT DIMENSIONS AND EXPANSION FRONTIER\n99: - Completed pivots: 0\n100: - Failed pivots: 0\n101: - Audited overrides: 0\n102: - Swept: none yet\n103: - Pivot lineage: none yet\n104: - Remaining frontier: none recorded\n105: \n106: ## 11. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\n107: \n108: - `/create:skill-parent` reduced to `/create:skill`: ruled out — `-` is a continuation character, and `/create:skill-x` returns no command (iteration 1, evidence: executed `typedCommandIn`).\n109: - Typed command overwritten by compiled enrichment: ruled out by call order at `handlers/advisor-recommend.ts:624-629,699-704` (iteration 1).\n110: - Stale attached command served from cache: ruled out — only the pre-enrichment output is cached and enrichment reruns on a hit (iteration 1).\n111: - `/doctor:install` mislabelled read-only: ruled out against `install.md:5` and the route's `gate3_location` n/a (iteration 2).\n112: - A `mutates` doctor route offered by name through the helper hand-off: ruled out by the `policy === 'run'` filter in `runnableDoctorBridgeId` (iteration 2).\n113: - `COMMAND_POLICIES` and `TRACKED_COMMANDS` disagreeing: ruled out by executed comparison, 0 mismatches (iteration 2).\n114: - Holdout rows leaking through `advisor_status`: ruled out — the status surface reports vector counts, not prompts (iteration 2).\n115: \n116: ---\n117: \n118: <!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n119: ## 11. NEXT FOCUS\n120: - Dimension: none remaining\n121: - Focus area: synthesis complete; report at `review-report.md`\n122: - Reason: convergence reached at iteration 5 of 5 with no active P0 or P1\n123: - Rotation status: complete\n124: - Blocked/productive carry-forward: no blocked approaches; correctness and security were the productive dimensions\n125: - Required evidence: the findings registry, the five iteration records, and the report\n126: <!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n127: ## 13. KNOWN CONTEXT\n128: \n129: ### Bounded Context Snapshot\n130: \n131: - Target pointers: `lib/command-attach.ts` (generated `MODE_COMMANDS`, `COMMAND_ROWS`,\n132:   `COMMAND_POLICIES`, `TRACKED_COMMANDS`; `attachCommand`, `typedCommandForTop`, `routeNeedsMode`),\n133:   `handlers/advisor-recommend.ts` (`enrichCompiledRoutes`, `attachTypedCommand`, `publicRecommendation`),\n134:   `lib/scorer/fusion.ts` (`requireCommandPhraseAnchor`, `commandMeaningEligible`, `readOnlyRouteAllowed`,\n135:   `applyDoctorHelperHandoff`, `rankTypedCommandOwnerFirst`), `lib/scorer/ambiguity.ts`,\n136:   `lib/scorer/doctor-helper-handoff.ts`, `schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts`,\n137:   `runtime/scripts/command-bridges/*`, `feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/*.md`,\n138:   shared `README.md` / `ARCHITECTURE.md` for the advisor.\n139: - Behavior claims: a single-mode compiled route attaches the hub's slash command; a typed command\n140:   travels through its owner only; policy is `run` only for a read-only or spec-folder-confined\n141:   add-only command; a mutating command is never offered with `run`; a meaning-passed command row\n142:   needs a real cosine of 0.72 and a 0.02 lead; a no-edit prompt rules out every command.\n143: - Reuse and conventions: generated blocks are deriver output, never hand-edited; generated data is\n144:   drift-guarded by `command-bridges-drift-guard.vitest.ts`; `review-core.md` severity/evidence rules.\n145: - Review risks and gaps: `resource-map.md` absent (coverage gate skipped); holdout-bearing scripts\n146:   live outside this lineage; the router's mode selection is an upstream input that was not executed\n147:   (no write-safe way to probe it), so route-dependent findings state the reach condition.\n148: - Out of scope: doctor implementations, hook renderers, accuracy runner, compiled-routing engine.\n149: \n150: ---\n151: \n152: ## 14. CROSS-REFERENCE STATUS\n153: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n154: [Alignment checks completed across core and overlay protocols]\n155: \n156: | Protocol | Level | Status | Iteration | Notes |\n157: |----------|-------|--------|-----------|-------|\n158: | `spec_code` | core | partial | 1 | Route-derived command attachment matches the documented contract except the two P2 deviations recorded in iteration 1. |\n159: | `checklist_evidence` | core | pending | - | No packet checklist claims were in iteration 1's focus. |\n160: | `skill_agent` | overlay | pending | - | - |\n161: | `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | pending | - | - |\n162: | `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | pending | - | - |\n163: | `playbook_capability` | overlay | notApplicable | - | no playbook path in this surface |\n164: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n165: \n166: ---\n167: \n168: ## 15. FILES UNDER REVIEW\n169: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n170: [Per-file coverage state table -- populated during initialization from scope discovery]\n171: \n172: | File | Dimensions Reviewed | Last Iteration | Findings | Status |\n173: |------|-------------------|----------------|----------|--------|\n174: | `lib/command-attach.ts` | correctness | 1 | 0 P0, 0 P1, 2 P2 | partial |\n175: | `handlers/advisor-recommend.ts` | correctness | 1 | 0 P0, 0 P1, 0 P2 | partial |\n176: | `lib/scorer/fusion.ts` | correctness (typed-owner ordering) | 1 | 0 P0, 0 P1, 0 P2 | partial |\n177: | `tests/command-attach.vitest.ts` | correctness (case inventory) | 1 | 0 P0, 0 P1, 0 P2 | partial |\n178: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n179: \n180: ---\n181: \n182: ## 16. REVIEW BOUNDARIES\n183: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n184: - Max iterations: 5\n185: