{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794570402658,"sessionID":"ses_e2b4a23c4ffeXM7ei3r7kNeMRl","part":{"partID":"prt_1d4bb39c0001himdk2uqpUKosq","sessionID":"ses_e2b4a23c4ffeXM7ei3r7kNeMRl","messageID":"msg_1d4bb174d001mQUXVjobUqOtRj","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8ad2885b72909916","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts","offset":660,"limit":180},"output":"Read file .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts, lines 660-839\n660: }\n661: \n662: function hasExplicitWorkflowSignal(contributions: readonly LaneContribution[], skillId: string): boolean {\n663:   const explicit = contributions.find((contribution) => contribution.lane === 'explicit_author');\n664:   if (!explicit || explicit.rawScore < EXPLICIT_WORKFLOW_SIGNAL_FLOOR) return false;\n665:   return explicit.evidence.some((entry) => (\n666:     entry.startsWith('phrase:')\n667:     || entry.startsWith('explicit:')\n668:     || entry.startsWith('author:')\n669:     || entry.includes(skillId)\n670:     || entry.includes('loop')\n671:     || entry.includes('write-')\n672:   ));\n673: }\n674: \n675: export function readOnlyRouteAllowed(promptLower: string, skill: SkillProjection): boolean {\n676:   const skillId = skill.id;\n677:   if (NO_EDIT_REQUEST.test(promptLower)) {\n678:     return false;\n679:   }\n680:   // The explainer floor exists to stop an ambiguous read-only question from\n681:   // routing anywhere. Naming the skill removes the ambiguity: the caller has\n682:   // already chosen, and a read-only verb does not undo that choice. Without\n683:   // this, an explicit request is answered with an abstention while the same\n684:   // sentence phrased with a write verb routes fine.\n685:   if (promptMentionsSkill(promptLower, skill)) {\n686:     return true;\n687:   }\n688:   // A command whose route only reads (a report, a status check) is the answer\n689:   // to a list or show question, so its own trigger phrase lifts it off the\n690:   // floor. A mutating command never carries the flag and stays gated.\n691:   if (skill.kind === 'command' && 'readOnly' in skill && skill.readOnly === true\n692:     && skill.keywords.some((phrase) => matchesPhraseBoundary(promptLower, phrase.toLowerCase()))) {\n693:     return true;\n694:   }\n695:   if (skillId === 'sk-code' && /\\b(compare|audit|review)\\b/.test(promptLower)\n696:     && /\\b(classifier|vocabulary|prose|implementation|agents\\.md|drift|mismatch)\\b/.test(promptLower)) {\n697:     return true;\n698:   }\n699:   if (skillId === 'system-spec-kit' && /\\b(memory_save|resume_write|routing taxonomy|corpus|source-type|routing bucket)\\b/.test(promptLower)) {\n700:     return true;\n701:   }\n702:   if (skillId === 'system-spec-kit' && /\\b(packet|spec folder|save memory|phase|continuation prompts|resume handling)\\b/.test(promptLower)) {\n703:     return true;\n704:   }\n705:   // Captured operator answers wait in a queue that spec-kit's save step owns, so a show or list\n706:   // question about that queue, its chat candidates or the decision record is answered there.\n707:   // Only a read-only question is lifted: a lift applies to any prompt, and a request to research,\n708:   // dispatch or build something about decisions belongs to another skill.\n709:   if (skillId === 'system-spec-kit' && isReadOnlyExplainer(promptLower)\n710:     && /\\b(decision capture|decision record|chat candidates?|operator decisions?|recorded as decisions?)\\b/.test(promptLower)) {\n711:     return true;\n712:   }\n713:   // The trigger index is spec-kit's own lookup surface, so a question about what a lookup\n714:   // returned, counted or left out is answered there. Without the lift no skill passes on such a\n715:   // question, and the doctor hand-off claims it on the index noun alone. Drift is the doctor's\n716:   // own diagnosis, so a drift question stays with the hand-off.\n717:   if (skillId === 'system-spec-kit' && isReadOnlyExplainer(promptLower)\n718:     && /\\btrigger[- ]index\\b/.test(promptLower) && !/\\bdrift\\b/.test(promptLower)) {\n719:     return true;\n720:   }\n721:   if (skillId === 'system-deep-loop' && /\\b(ai council|planning council|council deliberation|council artifacts|multi-seat planning)\\b/.test(promptLower)) {\n722:     return true;\n723:   }\n724:   // Browser/devtools inspection is a genuine chrome-devtools task even though\n725:   // its verb (\"inspect\") reads as a read-only explainer. Lift it off the\n726:   // explainer floor when the prompt carries devtools-specific vocabulary.\n727:   if (skillId === 'mcp-tooling'\n728:     && /\\b(network waterfall|network tab|network request|dev ?tools|browser console|page inspector|dom inspector|performance trace|inspect (the )?(network|dom|page|element|browser))\\b/.test(promptLower)) {\n729:     return true;\n730:   }\n731:   if (skillId === 'sk-code' && /\\bgate-3-classifier\\.ts\\b/.test(promptLower)) {\n732:     return true;\n733:   }\n734:   return false;\n735: }\n736: \n737: function isPlainFileSavePrompt(promptLower: string): boolean {\n738:   return FILE_SAVE_OPERATION.test(promptLower) && !MEMORY_SAVE_CONTEXT_ANCHOR.test(promptLower.replace(/\\bfile(s)?\\b/g, ''));\n739: }\n740: \n741: function primaryIntentBonus(\n742:   promptLower: string,\n743:   recommendation: AdvisorScoredRecommendation,\n744: ): number {\n745:   const R = SCORING_CALIBRATION.routing;\n746:   if (/\\bdeep[- ]review\\b/.test(promptLower)) {\n747:     if (recommendation.skill === 'sk-code') {\n748:       return AUTHORS_CODE.test(promptLower) ? R.deepReviewCodeAuthoringSkCodeBonus : R.deepReviewSkCodeReviewPenalty;\n749:     }\n750:   }\n751:   if (/\\bdeep[- ]research\\b/.test(promptLower)) {\n752:     if (recommendation.skill === 'system-spec-kit' || recommendation.skill === 'sk-code') return R.deepResearchOtherSkillsPenalty;\n753:   }\n754:   if (DEEP_RESEARCH_CYCLE.test(promptLower)) {\n755:     if (recommendation.skill === 'system-spec-kit' || recommendation.skill === 'sk-code') return R.deepResearchCycleOtherSkillsPenalty;\n756:   }\n757:   if (/\\b(compare|audit|review)\\b/.test(promptLower) && /\\b(classifier|vocabulary|prose|implementation|agents\\.md|drift|mismatch)\\b/.test(promptLower)) {\n758:     if (recommendation.skill === 'sk-code') return R.compareAuditCodeReviewBonus;\n759:   }\n760:   // A changelog request that names its packet or spec folder still asks for a\n761:   // changelog, so sk-doc must outrank the spec workflow that \"spec folder\" lifts.\n762:   // Only those two skills are adjusted here. Every other skill falls through so\n763:   // later rules such as save-context or /speckit:plan still apply to it.\n764:   const changelogFromPacket = CHANGELOG_AUTHORING.test(promptLower)\n765:     && CHANGELOG_PACKET_SOURCE.test(promptLower)\n766:     && !AUTHORS_CODE.test(promptLower);\n767:   if (changelogFromPacket) {\n768:     if (recommendation.skill === 'sk-doc') return R.changelogFromPacketSkDocBonus;\n769:     if (recommendation.skill === 'system-spec-kit') return R.changelogFromPacketSpecKitPenalty;\n770:   }\n771:   // The corpus-study rule reads \"packet-local\" as study vocabulary, so it must\n772:   // stay off a changelog request or it would pull the prompt to system-spec-kit.\n773:   // \"packet-local changelog\" names sk-doc's changelog mode with or without an\n774:   // authoring verb, so packet-local is study vocabulary only when it qualifies\n775:   // something other than a changelog.\n776:   if (!changelogFromPacket && /\\b(corpus ids?|first-100 predictions|continuation prompts|routing study config|confusion matrix|source-mix note|prompt template|packet-local(?!\\s+changelog))\\b/.test(promptLower) && !AUTHORS_CODE.test(promptLower)) {\n777:     if (recommendation.skill === 'system-spec-kit') return R.corpusStudySpecKitBonus;\n778:     if (recommendation.skill === 'sk-prompt' || recommendation.skill === 'mcp-tooling' || recommendation.skill === 'sk-doc') return R.corpusStudyOtherSkillsPenalty;\n779:   }\n780:   if (promptLower.includes('/speckit:resume')) {\n781:     if (recommendation.skill === 'system-spec-kit') return R.speckitResumeSpecKitBonus;\n782:     if (recommendation.skill === 'command-speckit-resume') return R.speckitResumeCommandPenalty;\n783:   }\n784:   if (promptLower.includes('/speckit:plan')) {\n785:     if (recommendation.skill === 'command-speckit-plan') return R.speckitPlanCommandBonus;\n786:     if (recommendation.skill === 'sk-doc') return R.speckitPlanSkDocPenalty;\n787:   }\n788:   // External-tool-chain (\"call_tool_chain\") vocabulary belongs to mcp-code-mode,\n789:   // not the generic code skill. Disambiguate so the best guess for these\n790:   // toolchain-shaped prompts is mcp-code-mode.\n791:   // Toolchain + external-data-source vocabulary (webflow CMS, cms collection)\n792:   // is mcp-code-mode territory, not the generic code skill.\n793:   if (/\\b(call_tool_chain|code mode|tool ?chain|api chain|webflow cms|cms collection)\\b/.test(promptLower)) {\n794:     if (recommendation.skill === 'mcp-code-mode') return R.mcpToolchainCodeModeBonus;\n795:     if (recommendation.skill === 'sk-code') return R.mcpToolchainSkCodePenalty;\n796:   }\n797:   // A \"code audit\" is a single-pass code-review task, not a deep-review loop, so\n798:   // sk-code should win the near-tie this phrase produces. The sk-code bonus\n799:   // carries that; the deep-loop skills intentionally hold no \"code audit\"\n800:   // vocabulary, so they need no counter-penalty here.\n801:   if (/\\bcode audit\\b/.test(promptLower)) {\n802:     if (recommendation.skill === 'sk-code') return R.codeAuditCodeReviewBonus;\n803:   }\n804:   // Colon-command review-loop syntax (\":review:auto\") invokes the deep-review\n805:   // loop; rank it above single-pass code review.\n806:   if (/:review:(auto|confirm)\\b/.test(promptLower)) {\n807:     if (recommendation.skill === 'system-deep-loop') return R.reviewLoopDeepReviewBonus;\n808:     if (recommendation.skill === 'sk-code') return R.deepReviewSkCodeReviewPenalty;\n809:   }\n810:   // Auditing recommendation quality is a review task, not an advisor-self task.\n811:   if (/\\baudit\\b/.test(promptLower) && /\\b(recommendation|recommendations|recommendation quality|routing quality)\\b/.test(promptLower)) {\n812:     if (recommendation.skill === 'sk-code') return R.auditRecsCodeReviewBonus;\n813:     // Auditing routing output is a review task, not an advisor invocation: demote\n814:     // the advisor and its alias (the canonical self-rec id set) so neither ranks\n815:     // itself first here.\n816:     if (isAdvisorSelfRecommendationSkill(recommendation.skill)) return R.auditRecsAdvisorPenalty;\n817:   }\n818:   if (/\\b(save context|save memory)\\b/.test(promptLower)) {\n819:     if (recommendation.skill === 'command-speckit-save') return R.saveContextMemorySaveBonus;\n820:     if (recommendation.skill === 'system-spec-kit') return R.saveContextMemorySpecKitPenalty;\n821:   }\n822:   if (/\\b(create (a )?new agent|create agent)\\b/.test(promptLower) || promptLower.includes('/create:agent')) {\n823:     if (recommendation.skill === 'create:agent') return R.createAgentCreateAgentBonus;\n824:     if (recommendation.skill === 'sk-doc') return R.createAgentSkDocPenalty;\n825:   }\n826:   if (/\\bcreate (a )?(test|testing) playbook\\b/.test(promptLower) || promptLower.includes('/create:manual-testing-playbook')) {\n827:     if (recommendation.skill === 'create:manual-testing-playbook' || recommendation.skill === 'command-create-manual-testing-playbook') return R.createTestingPlaybookBonus;\n828:     if (recommendation.skill === 'sk-doc') return R.createTestingPlaybookSkDocPenalty;\n829:     if (recommendation.skill === 'system-deep-loop') return R.createTestingPlaybookOtherSkillsPenalty;\n830:   }\n831:   if (/\\bphase folder\\b/.test(promptLower)) {\n832:     if (recommendation.skill === 'system-spec-kit') return R.phaseFolderSpecKitBonus;\n833:   }\n834:   return 0;\n835: }\n836: \n837: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n838: // 5. CORE LOGIC\n839: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 840]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts, lines 660-839\n660: }\n661: \n662: function hasExplicitWorkflowSignal(contributions: readonly LaneContribution[], skillId: string): boolean {\n663:   const explicit = contributions.find((contribution) => contribution.lane === 'explicit_author');\n664:   if (!explicit || explicit.rawScore < EXPLICIT_WORKFLOW_SIGNAL_FLOOR) return false;\n665:   return explicit.evidence.some((entry) => (\n666:     entry.startsWith('phrase:')\n667:     || entry.startsWith('explicit:')\n668:     || entry.startsWith('author:')\n669:     || entry.includes(skillId)\n670:     || entry.includes('loop')\n671:     || entry.includes('write-')\n672:   ));\n673: }\n674: \n675: export function readOnlyRouteAllowed(promptLower: string, skill: SkillProjection): boolean {\n676:   const skillId = skill.id;\n677:   if (NO_EDIT_REQUEST.test(promptLower)) {\n678:     return false;\n679:   }\n680:   // The explainer floor exists to stop an ambiguous read-only question from\n681:   // routing anywhere. Naming the skill removes the ambiguity: the caller has\n682:   // already chosen, and a read-only verb does not undo that choice. Without\n683:   // this, an explicit request is answered with an abstention while the same\n684:   // sentence phrased with a write verb routes fine.\n685:   if (promptMentionsSkill(promptLower, skill)) {\n686:     return true;\n687:   }\n688:   // A command whose route only reads (a report, a status check) is the answer\n689:   // to a list or show question, so its own trigger phrase lifts it off the\n690:   // floor. A mutating command never carries the flag and stays gated.\n691:   if (skill.kind === 'command' && 'readOnly' in skill && skill.readOnly === true\n692:     && skill.keywords.some((phrase) => matchesPhraseBoundary(promptLower, phrase.toLowerCase()))) {\n693:     return true;\n694:   }\n695:   if (skillId === 'sk-code' && /\\b(compare|audit|review)\\b/.test(promptLower)\n696:     && /\\b(classifier|vocabulary|prose|implementation|agents\\.md|drift|mismatch)\\b/.test(promptLower)) {\n697:     return true;\n698:   }\n699:   if (skillId === 'system-spec-kit' && /\\b(memory_save|resume_write|routing taxonomy|corpus|source-type|routing bucket)\\b/.test(promptLower)) {\n700:     return true;\n701:   }\n702:   if (skillId === 'system-spec-kit' && /\\b(packet|spec folder|save memory|phase|continuation prompts|resume handling)\\b/.test(promptLower)) {\n703:     return true;\n704:   }\n705:   // Captured operator answers wait in a queue that spec-kit's save step owns, so a show or list\n706:   // question about that queue, its chat candidates or the decision record is answered there.\n707:   // Only a read-only question is lifted: a lift applies to any prompt, and a request to research,\n708:   // dispatch or build something about decisions belongs to another skill.\n709:   if (skillId === 'system-spec-kit' && isReadOnlyExplainer(promptLower)\n710:     && /\\b(decision capture|decision record|chat candidates?|operator decisions?|recorded as decisions?)\\b/.test(promptLower)) {\n711:     return true;\n712:   }\n713:   // The trigger index is spec-kit's own lookup surface, so a question about what a lookup\n714:   // returned, counted or left out is answered there. Without the lift no skill passes on such a\n715:   // question, and the doctor hand-off claims it on the index noun alone. Drift is the doctor's\n716:   // own diagnosis, so a drift question stays with the hand-off.\n717:   if (skillId === 'system-spec-kit' && isReadOnlyExplainer(promptLower)\n718:     && /\\btrigger[- ]index\\b/.test(promptLower) && !/\\bdrift\\b/.test(promptLower)) {\n719:     return true;\n720:   }\n721:   if (skillId === 'system-deep-loop' && /\\b(ai council|planning council|council deliberation|council artifacts|multi-seat planning)\\b/.test(promptLower)) {\n722:     return true;\n723:   }\n724:   // Browser/devtools inspection is a genuine chrome-devtools task even though\n725:   // its verb (\"inspect\") reads as a read-only explainer. Lift it off the\n726:   // explainer floor when the prompt carries devtools-specific vocabulary.\n727:   if (skillId === 'mcp-tooling'\n728:     && /\\b(network waterfall|network tab|network request|dev ?tools|browser console|page inspector|dom inspector|performance trace|inspect (the )?(network|dom|page|element|browser))\\b/.test(promptLower)) {\n729:     return true;\n730:   }\n731:   if (skillId === 'sk-code' && /\\bgate-3-classifier\\.ts\\b/.test(promptLower)) {\n732:     return true;\n733:   }\n734:   return false;\n735: }\n736: \n737: function isPlainFileSavePrompt(promptLower: string): boolean {\n738:   return FILE_SAVE_OPERATION.test(promptLower) && !MEMORY_SAVE_CONTEXT_ANCHOR.test(promptLower.replace(/\\bfile(s)?\\b/g, ''));\n739: }\n740: \n741: function primaryIntentBonus(\n742:   promptLower: string,\n743:   recommendation: AdvisorScoredRecommendation,\n744: ): number {\n745:   const R = SCORING_CALIBRATION.routing;\n746:   if (/\\bdeep[- ]review\\b/.test(promptLower)) {\n747:     if (recommendation.skill === 'sk-code') {\n748:       return AUTHORS_CODE.test(promptLower) ? R.deepReviewCodeAuthoringSkCodeBonus : R.deepReviewSkCodeReviewPenalty;\n749:     }\n750:   }\n751:   if (/\\bdeep[- ]research\\b/.test(promptLower)) {\n752:     if (recommendation.skill === 'system-spec-kit' || recommendation.skill === 'sk-code') return R.deepResearchOtherSkillsPenalty;\n753:   }\n754:   if (DEEP_RESEARCH_CYCLE.test(promptLower)) {\n755:     if (recommendation.skill === 'system-spec-kit' || recommendation.skill === 'sk-code') return R.deepResearchCycleOtherSkillsPenalty;\n756:   }\n757:   if (/\\b(compare|audit|review)\\b/.test(promptLower) && /\\b(classifier|vocabulary|prose|implementation|agents\\.md|drift|mismatch)\\b/.test(promptLower)) {\n758:     if (recommendation.skill === 'sk-code') return R.compareAuditCodeReviewBonus;\n759:   }\n760:   // A changelog request that names its packet or spec folder still asks for a\n761:   // changelog, so sk-doc must outrank the spec workflow that \"spec folder\" lifts.\n762:   // Only those two skills are adjusted here. Every other skill falls through so\n763:   // later rules such as save-context or /speckit:plan still apply to it.\n764:   const changelogFromPacket = CHANGELOG_AUTHORING.test(promptLower)\n765:     && CHANGELOG_PACKET_SOURCE.test(promptLower)\n766:     && !AUTHORS_CODE.test(promptLower);\n767:   if (changelogFromPacket) {\n768:     if (recommendation.skill === 'sk-doc') return R.changelogFromPacketSkDocBonus;\n769:     if (recommendation.skill === 'system-spec-kit') return R.changelogFromPacketSpecKitPenalty;\n770:   }\n771:   // The corpus-study rule reads \"packet-local\" as study vocabulary, so it must\n772:   // stay off a changelog request or it would pull the prompt to system-spec-kit.\n773:   // \"packet-local changelog\" names sk-doc's changelog mode with or without an\n774:   // authoring verb, so packet-local is study vocabulary only when it qualifies\n775:   // something other than a changelog.\n776:   if (!changelogFromPacket && /\\b(corpus ids?|first-100 predictions|continuation prompts|routing study config|confusion matrix|source-mix note|prompt template|packet-local(?!\\s+changelog))\\b/.test(promptLower) && !AUTHORS_CODE.test(promptLower)) {\n777:     if (recommendation.skill === 'system-spec-kit') return R.corpusStudySpecKitBonus;\n778:     if (recommendation.skill === 'sk-prompt' || recommendation.skill === 'mcp-tooling' || recommendation.skill === 'sk-doc') return R.corpusStudyOtherSkillsPenalty;\n779:   }\n780:   if (promptLower.includes('/speckit:resume')) {\n781:     if (recommendation.skill === 'system-spec-kit') return R.speckitResumeSpecKitBonus;\n782:     if (recommendation.skill === 'command-speckit-resume') return R.speckitResumeCommandPenalty;\n783:   }\n784:   if (promptLower.includes('/speckit:plan')) {\n785:     if (recommendation.skill === 'command-speckit-plan') return R.speckitPlanCommandBonus;\n786:     if (recommendation.skill === 'sk-doc') return R.speckitPlanSkDocPenalty;\n787:   }\n788:   // External-tool-chain (\"call_tool_chain\") vocabulary belongs to mcp-code-mode,\n789:   // not the generic code skill. Disambiguate so the best guess for these\n790:   // toolchain-shaped prompts is mcp-code-mode.\n791:   // Toolchain + external-data-source vocabulary (webflow CMS, cms collection)\n792:   // is mcp-code-mode territory, not the generic code skill.\n793:   if (/\\b(call_tool_chain|code mode|tool ?chain|api chain|webflow cms|cms collection)\\b/.test(promptLower)) {\n794:     if (recommendation.skill === 'mcp-code-mode') return R.mcpToolchainCodeModeBonus;\n795:     if (recommendation.skill === 'sk-code') return R.mcpToolchainSkCodePenalty;\n796:   }\n797:   // A \"code audit\" is a single-pass code-review task, not a deep-review loop, so\n798:   // sk-code should win the near-tie this phrase produces. The sk-code bonus\n799:   // carries that; the deep-loop skills intentionally hold no \"code audit\"\n800:   // vocabulary, so they need no counter-penalty here.\n801:   if (/\\bcode audit\\b/.test(promptLower)) {\n802:     if (recommendation.skill === 'sk-code') return R.codeAuditCodeReviewBonus;\n803:   }\n804:   // Colon-command review-loop syntax (\":review:auto\") invokes the deep-review\n805:   // loop; rank it above single-pass code review.\n806:   if (/:review:(auto|confirm)\\b/.test(promptLower)) {\n807:     if (recommendation.skill === 'system-deep-loop') return R.reviewLoopDeepReviewBonus;\n808:     if (recommendation.skill === 'sk-code') return R.deepReviewSkCodeReviewPenalty;\n809:   }\n810:   // Auditing recommendation quality is a review task, not an advisor-self task.\n811:   if (/\\baudit\\b/.test(promptLower) && /\\b(recommendation|recommendations|recommendation quality|routing quality)\\b/.test(promptLower)) {\n812:     if (recommendation.skill === 'sk-code') return R.auditRecsCodeReviewBonus;\n813:     // Auditing routing output is a review task, not an advisor invocation: demote\n814:     // the advisor and its alias (the canonical self-rec id set) so neither ranks\n815:     // itself first here.\n816:     if (isAdvisorSelfRecommendationSkill(recommendation.skill)) return R.auditRecsAdvisorPenalty;\n817:   }\n818:   if (/\\b(save context|save memory)\\b/.test(promptLower)) {\n819:     if (recommendation.skill === 'command-speckit-save') return R.saveContextMemorySaveBonus;\n820:     if (recommendation.skill === 'system-spec-kit') return R.saveContextMemorySpecKitPenalty;\n821:   }\n822:   if (/\\b(create (a )?new agent|create agent)\\b/.test(promptLower) || promptLower.includes('/create:agent')) {\n823:     if (recommendation.skill === 'create:agent') return R.createAgentCreateAgentBonus;\n824:     if (recommendation.skill === 'sk-doc') return R.createAgentSkDocPenalty;\n825:   }\n826:   if (/\\bcreate (a )?(test|testing) playbook\\b/.test(promptLower) || promptLower.includes('/create:manual-testing-playbook')) {\n827:     if (recommendation.skill === 'create:manual-testing-playbook' || recommendation.skill === 'command-create-manual-testing-playbook') return R.createTestingPlaybookBonus;\n828:     if (recommendation.skill === 'sk-doc') return R.createTestingPlaybookSkDocPenalty;\n829:     if (recommendation.skill === 'system-deep-loop') return R.createTestingPlaybookOtherSkillsPenalty;\n830:   }\n831:   if (/\\bphase folder\\b/.test(promptLower)) {\n832:     if (recommendation.skill === 'system-spec-kit') return R.phaseFolderSpecKitBonus;\n833:   }\n834:   return 0;\n835: }\n836: \n837: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n838: // 5. CORE LOGIC\n839: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 840]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\": \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts\", \"offset\": 660, \"limit\": 180}"},"time":{"start":1794570402240,"end":1794570402658}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794570408493,"sessionID":"ses_e2b4a23c4ffeXM7ei3r7kNeMRl","part":{"partID":"prt_1d4bb35d2002r0y2n15yGwTAN7","sessionID":"ses_e2b4a23c4ffeXM7ei3r7kNeMRl","messageID":"msg_1d4bb174d001mQUXVjobUqOtRj","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-908c14af3c243cf0","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && rg -n \"COMMAND_POLICIES|commandPolicies\" --glob '!.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/**' -g '!**/node_modules/**' . | head -30"},"output":"./specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/decision-record.md:42:| Q006 | D1: a surfaced command that writes tracked files the user asked for is started, not asked about. | Not stated. | None | 007 research.md section 13, 002 commandPolicies |\n./specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/002-command-inventory-and-risk-metadata/spec.md:64:- A `commandPolicies` list in `command-bridges.generated.json`.\n./specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/002-command-inventory-and-risk-metadata/spec.md:103:- Derive a policy per command and per doctor route or action and emit it as `commandPolicies` in the generated file.\n./specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/002-command-inventory-and-risk-metadata/spec.md:120:| `ADV/scripts/command-bridges/command-bridges.generated.json` | Modify | Regenerated: four new disabled entries and `commandPolicies` |\n./specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/002-command-inventory-and-risk-metadata/spec.md:149:| REQ-006 | `command-bridges.generated.json` has a top-level `commandPolicies` array with one record per command and one per doctor route or action. A record has `command`, `route`, `mutating`, `askFirst` and `policy`. Each entry in `entries` keeps its six keys. |\n./specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/002-command-inventory-and-risk-metadata/spec.md:160:| REQ-012 | Rolled up to the strictest route per command, `commandPolicies` gives 7 `run`, 22 `start` and 15 `ask`, the counts in section 5 of the review. A command that lands elsewhere is listed with its reason in `implementation-summary.md`. |\n./specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/002-command-inventory-and-risk-metadata/spec.md:173:- **SC-001**: `node ADV/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs --check | jq -r .status` prints `fresh`, and `jq '[.commandPolicies[].command] | unique | length'` on the generated file prints 44.\n./specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/002-command-inventory-and-risk-metadata/plan.md:29:The deriver gains a tree read, two identity failures, attribute validation and a policy function, and it writes the result as a new top-level `commandPolicies` array. Five metadata files and the doctor manifest gain the risk keys, after the skill root metadata contract is amended to let a standalone root carry the file. The proof is `--check` printing `fresh`, a fixture test for the failures and the rule, and the phase 1 baseline rows holding still.\n./specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/002-command-inventory-and-risk-metadata/plan.md:63:- **`commandPolicies`**: a top-level array in the generated file. It sits outside `entries` because the drift guard compares each entry with a fixed key set, and outside the scorer blocks because nothing scores on it yet.\n./specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/002-command-inventory-and-risk-metadata/plan.md:189:| Deriver change and regeneration | The three above | `commandPolicies` and the identity check | Tests and the rollup |\n./specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/002-command-inventory-and-risk-metadata/plan.md:217:| M3 | Policies derived | `--check` prints `fresh` and the generated file lists 44 commands in `commandPolicies` | End of Implementation |\n\n[showing lines 20-30 of 30; full output saved to /Users/michelkerkmeester/.local/share/opencode/shell/4c10847297631c3af43d766cf1908920fe00c449/sh_1d4bb3b40001nzxDst8XKSO1eY.out]","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":true,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"./specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/decision-record.md:42:| Q006 | D1: a surfaced command that writes tracked files the user asked for is started, not asked about. | Not stated. | None | 007 research.md section 13, 002 commandPolicies |\n./specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/002-command-inventory-and-risk-metadata/spec.md:64:- A `commandPolicies` list in `command-bridges.generated.json`.\n./specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/002-command-inventory-and-risk-metadata/spec.md:103:- Derive a policy per command and per doctor route or action and emit it as `commandPolicies` in the generated file.\n./specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/002-command-inventory-and-risk-metadata/spec.md:120:| `ADV/scripts/command-bridges/command-bridges.generated.json` | Modify | Regenerated: four new disabled entries and `commandPolicies` |\n./specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/002-command-inventory-and-risk-metadata/spec.md:149:| REQ-006 | `command-bridges.generated.json` has a top-level `commandPolicies` array with one record per command and one per doctor route or action. A record has `command`, `route`, `mutating`, `askFirst` and `policy`. Each entry in `entries` keeps its six keys. |\n./specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/002-command-inventory-and-risk-metadata/spec.md:160:| REQ-012 | Rolled up to the strictest route per command, `commandPolicies` gives 7 `run`, 22 `start` and 15 `ask`, the counts in section 5 of the review. A command that lands elsewhere is listed with its reason in `implementation-summary.md`. |\n./specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/002-command-inventory-and-risk-metadata/spec.md:173:- **SC-001**: `node ADV/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs --check | jq -r .status` prints `fresh`, and `jq '[.commandPolicies[].command] | unique | length'` on the generated file prints 44.\n./specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/002-command-inventory-and-risk-metadata/plan.md:29:The deriver gains a tree read, two identity failures, attribute validation and a policy function, and it writes the result as a new top-level `commandPolicies` array. Five metadata files and the doctor manifest gain the risk keys, after the skill root metadata contract is amended to let a standalone root carry the file. The proof is `--check` printing `fresh`, a fixture test for the failures and the rule, and the phase 1 baseline rows holding still.\n./specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/002-command-inventory-and-risk-metadata/plan.md:63:- **`commandPolicies`**: a top-level array in the generated file. It sits outside `entries` because the drift guard compares each entry with a fixed key set, and outside the scorer blocks because nothing scores on it yet.\n./specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/002-command-inventory-and-risk-metadata/plan.md:189:| Deriver change and regeneration | The three above | `commandPolicies` and the identity check | Tests and the rollup |\n./specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/002-command-inventory-and-risk-metadata/plan.md:217:| M3 | Policies derived | `--check` prints `fresh` and the generated file lists 44 commands in `commandPolicies` | End of Implementation |\n\n[showing lines 20-30 of 30; full out