{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794570653036,"sessionID":"ses_e2b4a23c4ffeXM7ei3r7kNeMRl","part":{"partID":"prt_1d4bf03e1001G59vYKwCqmOIiF","sessionID":"ses_e2b4a23c4ffeXM7ei3r7kNeMRl","messageID":"msg_1d4befae8001QLiLHRnU6b7cx3","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b8533e7ded8dbd4a","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"newString":"## 8. WHAT WORKED\n\n- Locating each pass-one fix by content instead of by its cited line: deleting the `COMMAND_POLICIES` block shortened `command-attach.ts` by about 33 lines, so all three old line numbers were stale and a line-indexed re-read would have reported three phantom \"fix missing\" findings (iteration 1).\n- Running the changed guard file instead of reasoning about it: `command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` + `command-attach.vitest.ts` ran 24 tests green in 1.09s, which is the difference between \"the fix is present\" and \"the fix is pinned\" (iteration 1).\n- Reading the generator's row-emission function to check the deletion's blast radius: `renderCommandRows` throws on a duplicate or conflicting id, which is what makes the surviving generated table trustworthy after the deleted block (iteration 1).\n\n---\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n\n- Reading `command-attach.vitest.ts:118-121` as a gate assertion: the line passes a table that does not hold the requested mode, so it never reaches the gate. The reading failed, and the mismatch became finding `SA2-P2-001` rather than a false clean pass (iteration 1).","oldString":"## 8. WHAT WORKED\n\n- [First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n\n---\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n\n- [First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-2/deep-review-strategy.md"},"output":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-2/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metada