{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794570863572,"sessionID":"ses_e2b4a23c4ffeXM7ei3r7kNeMRl","part":{"partID":"prt_1d4c23e49001K46nuRCLHgmkHV","sessionID":"ses_e2b4a23c4ffeXM7ei3r7kNeMRl","messageID":"msg_1d4c22e6b001IRwU6HSIYiW1p8","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a22121ebaf9b9d44","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && sed -n '/ANCHOR:review-dimensions/,/\\/ANCHOR:running-findings/p' specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-2/deep-review-strategy.md; sed -n '/ANCHOR:next-focus/,/\\/ANCHOR:next-focus/p' specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-2/deep-review-strategy.md; sed -n '/FILES UNDER REVIEW/,/\\/MACHINE-OWNED: END/p' specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-2/deep-review-strategy.md | head -20"},"output":"<!-- ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n## 3. REVIEW DIMENSIONS (remaining)\n- [ ] security\n- [ ] traceability\n- [ ] maintainability\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n## 4. NON-GOALS\n\n- The doctor command implementations and route manifest content (`doctor-install` lineage owns them);\n  this lineage reads them only as context evidence for the derived policy table.\n- The hook renderers and session readers (`render-hooks-plugin` lineage owns them); `lib/render.ts`\n  is read only to confirm how a surfaced `policy` reaches a reader.\n- The accuracy runner, holdout builder and command transcript scorer (`accuracy-runner` owns them).\n  Holdout hygiene here means proving this lineage's own surface never reads, tunes on or prints\n  holdout rows; prompt text is never read or printed, counts only.\n- The compiled-routing engine internals (`.skilled/bin/lib/compiled-routing/**`); a route decision is\n  an input contract.\n- Pass-one findings outside this area, deferred items in the pass-one report section 8, `R4-P2-003`\n  and the refuted finding are not re-reported.\n- No code changes: review is observation-only.\n\n---\n\n## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n\n- Convergence: `newFindingsRatio` at or below `convergenceThreshold` 0.10 with no active P0/P1.\n- Cap: `maxIterations` 7.\n- Stuck: two consecutive iterations with no new evidence (stuckThreshold 2).\n- Any active P0 blocks PASS regardless of convergence.\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n## 4. COMPLETED DIMENSIONS\n- [x] correctness\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n<!-- ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n## 5. RUNNING FINDINGS\n- P0 (Blockers): 0\n- P1 (Required): 0\n- P2 (Suggestions): 1\n- Resolved: 0\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n<!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n## 11. NEXT FOCUS\n- Dimension: security - Focus area: safety of offering a mutating command — `TRACKED_COMMANDS` policy vs `mutating` class, `COMMAND_ROWS` rows whose policy is `run`, and the `policy`/`mutating` pair the recommend path emits (`advisor-recommend.ts:478-485`, `render.ts` consumption read only as context). - Reason: the pass-one area summary claimed no `run` row writes; that claim is the security-shaped fix surface and must be re-proven against the changed tables, not re-read from the old report. - Rotation status: correctness complete (PASS), security next. - Blocked/productive carry-forward: correctness was productive (one test-quality finding); no blocked approach. - Required evidence: executed whole-table invariant over `COMMAND_ROWS`, plus the recommend-path policy source. Review verdict: PASS\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n## 15. FILES UNDER REVIEW\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n[Per-file coverage state table -- populated as iterations complete]\n\n| File | Dimensions Reviewed | Last Iteration | Findings | Status |\n|------|-------------------|----------------|----------|--------|\n| `lib/command-attach.ts` | correctness | 1 | 0 P0, 0 P1, 0 P2 | complete |\n| `tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` | correctness | 1 | 0 P0, 0 P1, 0 P2 | complete |\n| `tests/command-attach.vitest.ts` | correctness | 1 | 0 P0, 0 P1, 1 P2 | complete |\n| `scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs:1100-1274` | correctness | 1 | 0 P0, 0 P1, 0 P2 | partial |\n| `lib/scorer/fusion.ts:660-839` | correctness | 1 | 0 P0, 0 P1, 0 P2 | partial |\n| `handlers/advisor-recommend.ts:420-539` | correctness | 1 | 0 P0, 0 P1, 0 P2 | partial |\n<!-- /MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"<!-- ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n## 3. REVIEW DIMENSIONS (remaining)\n- [ ] security\n- [ ] traceability\n- [ ] maintainability\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n## 4. NON-GOALS\n\n- The doctor command implementations and route manifest content (`doctor-install` lineage owns them);\n  this lineage reads them only as context evidence for the derived policy table.\n- The hook renderers and session readers (`render-hooks-plugin` lineage owns them); `lib/render.ts`\n  is read only to confirm how a surfaced `policy` reaches a reader.\n- The accuracy runner, holdout builder and command transcript scorer (`accuracy-runner` owns them).\n  Holdout hygiene here means proving this lineage's own surface never reads, tunes on or prints\n  holdout rows; prompt text is never read or printed, counts only.\n- The compiled-routing engine internals (`.skilled/bin/lib/compiled-routing/**`); a route decision is\n  an input contract.\n- Pass-one findings outside this area, deferred items in the pass-one report section 8, `R4-P2-003`\n  and the refuted finding are not re-reported.\n- No code changes: review is observation-only.\n\n---\n\n## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n\n- Convergence: `newFindingsRatio` at or below `convergenceThreshold` 0.10 with no active P0/P1.\n- Cap: `maxIterations` 7.\n- Stuck: two consecutive iterations with no new evidence (stuckThreshold 2).\n- Any active P0 blocks PASS regardless of convergence.\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n## 4. COMPLETED DIMENSIONS\n- [x] correctness\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n<!-- ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n## 5. RUNNING FINDINGS\n- P0 (Blockers): 0\n- P1 (Required): 0\n- P2 (Suggestions): 1\n- Resolved: 0\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n<!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n## 11. NEXT FOCUS\n- Dimension: security - Focus area: safety of offering a mutating command — `TRACKED_COMMANDS` policy vs `mutating` class, `COMMAND_ROWS` rows whose policy is `run`, and the `policy`/`mutating` pair the recommend path emits (`advisor-recommend.ts:478-485`, `render.ts` consumption read only as context). - Reason: the pass-one area summary claimed no `run` row writes; that claim is the security-shaped fix surface and must be re-proven against the changed tables, not re-read from the old report. - Rotation status: correctness complete (PASS), security next. - Blocked/productive carry-forward: correctness was productive (one test-quality finding); no blocked approach. - Required evidence: executed whole-table invariant over `COMMAND_ROWS`, plus the recommend-path policy source. Review verdict: PASS\n\n<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n## 15. FILES UNDER REVIEW\n<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n[Per-file coverage state table -- populated as iterations complete]\n\n| File | Dimensions Reviewed | Last Iteration | Findings | Status |\n|------|-------------------|----------------|----------|--------|\n| `lib/command-attach.ts` | correctness | 1 | 0 P0, 0 P1, 0 P2 | complete |\n| `tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` | correctness | 1 | 0 P0, 0 P1, 0 P2 | complete |\n| `tests/command-attach.vitest.ts` | correctness | 1 | 0 P0, 0 P1, 1 P2 | complete |\n| `scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs:1100-1274` | correctness | 1 | 0 P0, 0 P1, 0 P2 | partial |\n| `lib/scorer/fusion.ts:660-839` | correctness | 1 | 0 P0, 0 P1, 0 P2 | partial |\n| `handlers/advisor-recommend.ts:420-539` | correctness | 1 | 0 P0, 0 P1, 0 P2 | partial |\n<!-- /MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && sed -n '/ANCHOR:review-dimensions/,/\\\\/ANCHOR:running-findings/p' specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-2/deep-review-strategy.md; sed -n '/ANCHOR:next-focus/,/\\\\/ANCHOR:next-focus/p' specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-2/deep-review-strategy.md; sed -n '/FILES UNDER REVIEW/,/\\\\/MACHINE-OWNED: END/p' specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-2/deep-review-strategy.md | head -20\"}"},"time":{"start":1794570862153,"end":1794570863572}}}}
