{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794570956712,"sessionID":"ses_e2b4a23c4ffeXM7ei3r7kNeMRl","part":{"partID":"prt_1d4c3acb7002OKQDzaTyIpXsBQ","sessionID":"ses_e2b4a23c4ffeXM7ei3r7kNeMRl","messageID":"msg_1d4c38823001sEKOy1JqH52Y0C","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b2a3f5d7c6ffb62d","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -n \"46 rows\\|46 \" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/README.md | head -5; echo \"=== capture baseline real-embedding claims ===\"; grep -n \"nomic-embed-text\\|--write\\|vec_cmd\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs | head -12"},"output":"176:Command rows use the same embedder. The bridge deriver writes an `embeddingText` for each of the 46 command rows the TypeScript scorer serves, and `skill_graph_scan` embeds it into its own `vec_cmd_<dim>` table beside the skill vectors. The scan skips a row whose text has not changed and prunes a row that is no longer generated. A command row normally passes only on one of its own phrases or its slash string. It can also pass on meaning: the prompt's real embedding has to reach a cosine of 0.72 against the row and lead the next command row by 0.02. A command that passed this way ranks first only when it leads the top passing skill by the same 0.02. A prompt that asks for no change, such as \"no edits\" or \"just list\", rules out every command on meaning. A read-only question lets only a command whose route only reads pass on meaning. Without the local embedder (Ollama serving `nomic-embed-text`) no cosine exists, so command rows pass on their phrases alone.\n=== capture baseline real-embedding claims ===\n37://   node capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs --write    # also write the baseline\n89:const EMBEDDER_MODEL_PREFIX = 'nomic-embed-text';\n91:const COMMAND_VECTOR_TABLE_PREFIX = 'vec_cmd_';\n159:  // `vec_cmd_<dim>` family alone rather than any name shaped like it.\n676:  rejectUnknownOptions(import.meta.url, ['--write', '--real-embedding']);\n682:  if (realEmbedding && process.argv.includes('--write')) {\n683:    process.stderr.write('capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs: --write cannot be combined with --real-embedding; the committed baseline is captured under the fixture regime only\\n');\n690:    if (process.argv.includes('--write')) {\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"176:Command rows use the same embedder. The bridge deriver writes an `embeddingText` for each of the 46 command rows the TypeScript scorer serves, and `skill_graph_scan` embeds it into its own `vec_cmd_<dim>` table beside the skill vectors. The scan skips a row whose text has not changed and prunes a row that is no longer generated. A command row normally passes only on one of its own phrases or its slash string. It can also pass on meaning: the prompt's real embedding has to reach a cosine of 0.72 against the row and lead the next command row by 0.02. A command that passed this way ranks first only when it leads the top passing skill by the same 0.02. A prompt that asks for no change, such as \"no edits\" or \"just list\", rules out every command on meaning. A read-only question lets only a command whose route only reads pass on meaning. Without the local embedder (Ollama serving `nomic-embed-text`) no cosine exists, so command rows pass on their phrases alone.\n=== capture baseline real-embedding claims ===\n37://   node capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs --write    # also write the baseline\n89:const EMBEDDER_MODEL_PREFIX = 'nomic-embed-text';\n91:const COMMAND_VECTOR_TABLE_PREFIX = 'vec_cmd_';\n159:  // `vec_cmd_<dim>` family alone rather than any name shaped like it.\n676:  rejectUnknownOptions(import.meta.url, ['--write', '--real-embedding']);\n682:  if (realEmbedding && process.argv.includes('--write')) {\n683:    process.stderr.write('capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs: --write cannot be combined with --real-embedding; the committed baseline is captured under the fixture regime only\\n');\n690:    if (process.argv.includes('--write')) {\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -n \\\"46 rows\\\\|46 \\\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/README.md | head -5; echo \\\"=== capture baseline real-embedding claims ===\\\"; grep -n \\\"nomic-embed-text\\\\|--write\\\\|vec_cmd\\\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs | head -12\"}"},"time":{"start":1794570955959,"end":1794570956712}}}}
