{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794571199690,"sessionID":"ses_e2b4a23c4ffeXM7ei3r7kNeMRl","part":{"partID":"prt_1d4c761b5002BR6qoB4SCnDQf3","sessionID":"ses_e2b4a23c4ffeXM7ei3r7kNeMRl","messageID":"msg_1d4c73852001d6yNqniM52zbOp","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-910d082954a0eed3","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -rn \"compiledRouteTopOnly\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/ .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/ .opencode/plugins/ 2>/dev/null | head -10; echo \"=== deriver header ===\"; sed -n '1,60p' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs"},"output":".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/skill-advisor-cli-stale-daemon-retry.vitest.ts:127:      JSON.stringify({ prompt: 'Recommend a skill.', options: { includeCompiledRoute: false, compiledRouteTopOnly: true } }),\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/skill-advisor-cli-stale-daemon-retry.vitest.ts:178:    expect(Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(daemon.calls[1]?.options ?? {}, 'compiledRouteTopOnly')).toBe(false);\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/hooks/skill-advisor-cli-fallback-no-match.vitest.ts:93:        options?: { includeCompiledRoute?: boolean; compiledRouteTopOnly?: boolean };\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/hooks/skill-advisor-cli-fallback-no-match.vitest.ts:97:      expect(payload.options?.compiledRouteTopOnly).toBe(true);\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/handlers/README.md:46:| `advisor-recommend-compiled-route-option.vitest.ts` | Verifies that `includeCompiledRoute: false` skips enrichment on fresh and cached returns, that `compiledRouteTopOnly: true` looks up the route for the first recommendation alone and that a command ranking through its own row is not offered again by its hub. |\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/handlers/advisor-recommend-compiled-route-option.vitest.ts:121:      options: { includeCompiledRoute: true, compiledRouteTopOnly: true },\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/handlers/advisor-recommend-compiled-route-option.vitest.ts:180:      options: { includeCompiledRoute: true, compiledRouteTopOnly: true },\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/lib/README.md:21:| `skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts` | Resolves the CLI, IPC bridge and database paths from one root (`.skilled`, then `.opencode`), spawns the advisor CLI with a bounded timeout. It sends the request on stdin with `--json -`, so the prompt never appears in the child's argv. The request it sends carries `options.includeCompiledRoute: true`, because the advisor derives a recommendation's slash command from the compiled route, and `options.compiledRouteTopOnly: true`, so only the top pick gets a route lookup. `recommendationFromCli` keeps a non-empty `command` on each recommendation and reads nothing from the route itself. It runs the CLI with `--no-warm-only`, because the CLI is the component that starts the daemon on a cold socket. It parses its JSON payload and normalizes the result (and retryable exit/reason codes) into an `AdvisorHookResult`. |\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/lib/skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts:241:      compiledRouteTopOnly: true,\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md:38:4. **CLI front door.** The hook calls `buildSkillAdvisorBriefFromCli`, which runs `skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend --json - --no-warm-only` within the `SPECKIT_CLAUDE_HOOK_TIMEOUT_MS` budget (2,500 ms by default). It writes the request to the CLI's stdin, so the prompt never appears in the process table. The request carries at most the prompt's first 10,000 characters, the most `advisor_recommend` accepts, so a longer prompt is routed on its head instead of failing open. The Claude shim sets the child budget to 2,200 ms when the operator has not set the variable. An operator value above about 2,200 ms lets the shim kill the hook at 2,500 ms first, so the turn gets `{}`. The CLI owns the warm-daemon probe, starts the daemon when the socket is cold and falls back to the local Python scorer with a `degraded` result. The request carries `includeCompiledRoute: true`, because the advisor derives a recommendation's slash command from the compiled route. It also carries `compiledRouteTopOnly: true`, because each route lookup is a subprocess inside the hook's budget and the brief leads with the top pick. The hook keeps the `command` field and reads nothing from the route itself. A daemon still running an older build rejects these options with JSON-RPC `-32602`, and the CLI retries once without them.\n=== deriver header ===\n// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// MODULE: Derive Command Bridges\n// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n'use strict';\n\n// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// 1. IMPORTS\n// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nconst { existsSync, readFileSync, readdirSync, writeFileSync } = require('node:fs');\nconst { join, relative, resolve, sep } = require('node:path');\n\n// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// 2. CONSTANTS\n// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nconst COMMAND_BRIDGES_DIR = __dirname;\nconst REPO_ROOT = resolve(COMMAND_BRIDGES_DIR, '../../../../../..');\nconst SKILLS_ROOT = join(REPO_ROOT, '.skilled', 'skills');\n// One folder per command group, one Markdown file per command: the tree the\n// inventory identity check reads.\nconst COMMANDS_ROOT = join(REPO_ROOT, '.skilled', 'commands');\nconst DOCTOR_COMMANDS_DIR = join(COMMANDS_ROOT, 'doctor');\nconst DOCTOR_ROUTES_PATH = join(DOCTOR_COMMANDS_DIR, '_routes.yaml');\nconst COMPATIBILITY_PATH = join(COMMAND_BRIDGES_DIR, 'scoring-compatibility.json');\nconst OUTPUT_PATH = join(COMMAND_BRIDGES_DIR, 'command-bridges.generated.json');\nconst TS_PROJECTION_PATH = join(\n  SKILLS_ROOT,\n  'system-skill-advisor',\n  'runtime',\n  'lib',\n  'scorer',\n  'projection.ts',\n);\nconst PY_ADVISOR_PATH = join(\n  SKILLS_ROOT,\n  'system-skill-advisor',\n  'runtime',\n  'scripts',\n  'skill_advisor.py',\n);\nconst TS_GENERATED_START = '// BEGIN GENERATED COMMAND BRIDGES';\nconst TS_GENERATED_END = '// END GENERATED COMMAND BRIDGES';\nconst PY_GENERATED_START = '# BEGIN GENERATED COMMAND BRIDGES';\nconst PY_GENERATED_END = '# END GENERATED COMMAND BRIDGES';\nconst DOCTOR_PREFIX = 'command-doctor-';\nconst DOCTOR_MCP_COMMAND = '/doctor:mcp';\n\n// Closed vocabularies: an unrecognised value has to fail loudly, because a\n// silent fallthrough would hand a mutating command the read-only policy (or the\n// reverse) and nothing downstream would notice.\nconst MUTATING_CLASSES = ['read-only', 'add-only', 'mutates'];\nconst ASK_FIRST_REASONS = ['settings', 'outside-repo', 'spend', 'relaunch'];\nconst WRITE_SCOPES = ['spec-folder'];\n// A command with several routes and no target typed answers for its strictest\n// route, because the reader gave the bridge no way to narrow the run.\nconst POLICY_STRICTNESS = ['run', 'start', 'ask'];\n// A lead phrase outranks a passing skill, which is only safe when the prompt asks\n// about the state of something. A phrase that names no state or health word could\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/skill-advisor-cli-stale-daemon-retry.vitest.ts:127:      JSON.stringify({ prompt: 'Recommend a skill.', options: { includeCompiledRoute: false, compiledRouteTopOnly: true } }),\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/skill-advisor-cli-stale-daemon-retry.vitest.ts:178:    expect(Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(daemon.calls[1]?.options ?? {}, 'compiledRouteTopOnly')).toBe(false);\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/hooks/skill-advisor-cli-fallback-no-match.vitest.ts:93:        options?: { includeCompiledRoute?: boolean; compiledRouteTopOnly?: boolean };\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/hooks/skill-advisor-cli-fallback-no-match.vitest.ts:97:      expect(payload.options?.compiledRouteTopOnly).toBe(true);\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/handlers/README.md:46:| `advisor-recommend-compiled-route-option.vitest.ts` | Verifies that `includeCompiledRoute: false` skips enrichment on fresh and cached returns, that `compiledRouteTopOnly: true` looks up the route for the first recommendation alone and that a command ranking through its own row is not offered again by its hub. |\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/handlers/advisor-recommend-compiled-route-option.vitest.ts:121:      options: { includeCompiledRoute: true, compiledRouteTopOnly: true },\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/handlers/advisor-recommend-compiled-route-option.vitest.ts:180:      options: { includeCompiledRoute: true, compiledRouteTopOnly: true },\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/lib/README.md:21:| `skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts` | Resolves the CLI, IPC bridge and database paths from one root (`.skilled`, then `.opencode`), spawns the advisor CLI with a bounded timeout. It sends the request on stdin with `--json -`, so the prompt never appears in the child's argv. The request it sends carries `options.includeCompiledRoute: true`, because the advisor derives a recommendation's slash command from the compiled route, and `options.compiledRouteTopOnly: true`, so only the top pick gets a route lookup. `recommendationFromCli` keeps a non-empty `command` on each recommendation and reads nothing from the route itself. It runs the CLI with `--no-warm-only`, because the CLI is the component that starts the daemon on a cold socket. It parses its JSON payload and normalizes the result (and retryable exit/reason codes) into an `AdvisorHookResult`. |\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/lib/skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts:241:      compiledRouteTopOnly: true,\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/skill-advisor-hook.md:38:4. **CLI front door.** The hook calls `buildSkillAdvisorBriefFromCli`, which runs `skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend --json - --no-warm-only` within the `SPECKIT_CLAUDE_HOOK_TIMEOUT_MS` budget (2,500 ms by default). It writes the request to the CLI's stdin, so the prompt never appears in the process table. The request carries at most the prompt's first 10,000 characters, the most `advisor_recommend` accepts, so a longer prompt is routed on its head instead of failing open. The Claude shim sets the child budget to 2,200 ms when the operator has not set the variable. An operator value above about 2,200 ms lets the shim kill the hook at 2,500 ms first, so the turn gets `{}`. The CLI owns the warm-daemon probe, starts the daemon when the socket is cold and falls back to the local Python scorer with a `degraded` result. The request carries `includeCompiledRoute: true`, because the advisor derives a recommendation's slash command from the compiled route. It also carries `compiledRouteTopOnly: true`, because each route lookup is a subprocess inside the hook's budget and the brief leads with the top pick. The hook keeps the `command` field and reads nothing from the route itself. A daemon still running an older build rejects these options with JSON-RPC `-32602`, and the CLI retries once without them.\n=== deriver header ===\n// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// MODULE: Derive Command Bridges\n// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n'use strict';\n\n// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// 1. IMPORTS\n// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nconst { existsSync, readFileSync, readdirSync, writeFileSync } = require('node:fs');\nconst { join, relative, resolve, sep } = require('node:path');\n\n// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n// 2. CONSTANTS\n// ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\nconst COMMAND_BRIDGES_DIR = __dirname;\nconst REPO_ROOT = resolve(COMMAND_BRIDGES_DIR, '../../../../../..');\nconst SKILLS_ROOT = join(REPO_ROOT, '.skilled', 'skills');\n// One folder per command group, one Markdown file per command: the tree the\n// inventory identity check reads.\nconst COMMANDS_ROOT = join(REPO_ROOT, '.skilled', 'commands');\nconst DOCTOR_COMMANDS_DIR = join(COMMANDS_ROOT, 'doctor');\nconst DOCTOR_ROUTES_PATH = join(DOCTOR_COMMANDS_DIR, '_routes.yaml');\nconst COMPATIBILITY_PATH = join(COMMAND_BRIDGES_DIR, 'scoring-compatibility.json');\nconst OUTPUT_PATH = join(COMMAND_BRIDGES_DIR, 'command-bridges.generated.json');\nconst TS_PROJECTION_PATH = join(\n  SKILLS_ROOT,\n  'system-skill-advisor',\n  'runtime',\n  'lib',\n  'scorer',\n  'projection.ts',\n);\nconst PY_ADVISOR_PATH = join(\n  SKILLS_ROOT,\n  'system-skill-advisor',\n  'runtime',\n  'scripts',\n  'skill_advisor.py',\n);\nconst TS_GENERATED_START = '// BEGIN GENERATED COMMAND BRIDGES';\nconst TS_GENERATED_END = '// END GENERATED COMMAND BRIDGES';\nconst PY_GENERATED_START = '# BEGIN GENERATED COMMAND BRIDGES';\nconst PY_GENERATED_END = '# END GENERATED COMMAND BRIDGES';\nconst DOCTOR_PREFIX = 'command-doctor-';\nconst DOCTOR_MCP_COMMAND = '/doctor:mcp';\n\n// Closed vocabularies: an unrecognised value has to fail loudly, because a\n// silent fallthrough would hand a mutating command the read-only policy (or the\n// reverse) and nothing downstream would notice.\nconst MUTATING_CLASSES = ['read-only', 'add-only', 'mutates'];\nconst ASK_FIRST_REASONS = ['settings', 'outside-repo', 'spend', 'relaunch'];\nconst WRITE_SCOPES = ['spec-folder'];\n// A command with several routes and no target typed answers for its strictest\n// route, because the reader gave the bridge no way to narrow the run.\nconst POLICY_STRICTNESS = ['run', 'start', 'ask'];\n// A lead phrase outranks a passing skill, which is only safe when the prompt asks\n// about the state of something. A phrase that names no state or health word could\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -rn \\\"compiledRouteTopOnly\\\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/ .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/hooks/ .opencode/plugins/ 2>/dev/null | head -10; echo \\\"=== deriver header ===\\\"; sed -n '1,60p' .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs\"}"},"time":{"start":1794571198901,"end":1794571199690}}}}
