{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794571384015,"sessionID":"ses_e2b4a23c4ffeXM7ei3r7kNeMRl","part":{"partID":"prt_1d4ca30d4001rwhdOBQ2WhGTUE","sessionID":"ses_e2b4a23c4ffeXM7ei3r7kNeMRl","messageID":"msg_1d4ca1382001CnWFvRoe7zieXV","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a4de2701b7d52d22","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -n \"command-attach\\|MODE_COMMANDS\\|TRACKED_COMMANDS\\|command row\\|attach\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/ARCHITECTURE.md | head -12; echo \"=== diff stat ARCHITECTURE ===\"; git diff --stat 35c3188681..HEAD -- .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/ARCHITECTURE.md"},"output":"126:**Scorer.** Five lanes fuse into a single calibrated score: explicit author signals, lexical overlap, skill-graph causality, derived metadata, and a semantic shadow lane. The fusion respects per-lane weights and emits per-lane attribution alongside the final score. Command detail lives in `references/runtime/cli-front-door-contract.md`, and lane semantics live in `references/scoring/advisor-scorer.md`. Command rows get vectors of their own in a `vec_cmd_<dim>` table that the skill-graph scan fills from each row's generated `embeddingText`. The semantic lane's real cosine against those vectors is the second way a command row can pass, beside its own phrases. The pass needs a cosine of at least 0.72 and a 0.02 lead over the next command row. A no-edit prompt rules out every command on meaning, and a read-only question admits only a read-only command. With no live embedder the rule never fires.\n=== diff stat ARCHITECTURE ===\n .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/ARCHITECTURE.md | 8 ++++----\n 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"126:**Scorer.** Five lanes fuse into a single calibrated score: explicit author signals, lexical overlap, skill-graph causality, derived metadata, and a semantic shadow lane. The fusion respects per-lane weights and emits per-lane attribution alongside the final score. Command detail lives in `references/runtime/cli-front-door-contract.md`, and lane semantics live in `references/scoring/advisor-scorer.md`. Command rows get vectors of their own in a `vec_cmd_<dim>` table that the skill-graph scan fills from each row's generated `embeddingText`. The semantic lane's real cosine against those vectors is the second way a command row can pass, beside its own phrases. The pass needs a cosine of at least 0.72 and a 0.02 lead over the next command row. A no-edit prompt rules out every command on meaning, and a read-only question admits only a read-only command. With no live embedder the rule never fires.\n=== diff stat ARCHITECTURE ===\n .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/ARCHITECTURE.md | 8 ++++----\n 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -n \\\"command-attach\\\\|MODE_COMMANDS\\\\|TRACKED_COMMANDS\\\\|command row\\\\|attach\\\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/ARCHITECTURE.md | head -12; echo \\\"=== diff stat ARCHITECTURE ===\\\"; git diff --stat 35c3188681..HEAD -- .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/ARCHITECTURE.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794571382996,"end":1794571384015}}}}
